== Hostilities ==
{{further|Timeline of the 2026 Iran war|List of attacks during the 2026 Iran war}}
<!---Before adding new information to this section, please consider if it would be better suited to [[Timeline of the 2026 Iran war]] instead. This section should provide a broad overview. If you're unsure, add it to the timeline first and start a discussion on the Talk page about whether to include it here.--->

=== First week (28 February – 6 March) ===
{{Further|Assassination of Ali Khamenei|2026 Lebanon war|2026 Minab school attack|2026 Lamerd sports hall attack}}
[[File:U S Forces Launch Operation Epic Fury (9542157).jpg|thumb|27 February: US aircraft sit on the flight deck of {{USS|Abraham Lincoln|CVN-72|6}}]]
[[File:President Donald J. Trump on the United States Military Major Combat Operations in Iran.webm|thumb|28 February: Trump addresses the nation about the strikes.]]

On 27{{nbsp}}February at 3:38&nbsp;p.m. [[Eastern Time Zone#Eastern Standard Time|EST]] (11:08&nbsp;p.m. [[Iran Standard Time|IRST]]), Trump, traveling on [[Air Force One]] to [[Texas]], authorized Operation Epic Fury.<ref name="ii-epicfury">{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Pentagon Names Iran Mission 'Operation Epic Fury' |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202602280838 |website=[[Iran International]] |date=28 February 2026 |access-date=28 February 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260301040726/https://www.iranintl.com/en/202602280838 |archive-date=1 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="FT01">{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Inside the Plan to Kill Ali Khamenei |url=https://www.ft.com/content/bf998c69-ab46-4fa3-aae4-8f18f7387836 |work=[[Financial Times]] |access-date=3 March 2026 |language=en |date=2 March 2026}}</ref> US missiles, drones, and [[Israeli Air Force#Current inventory|Israeli fighter jets]] began striking Iran the next day, around 9:45&nbsp;a.m. IRST (1:15&nbsp;a.m. EST).<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/us-weapons-used-to-attack-iran-fend-off-retaliation-2026-2?IR=T |title=Here Are the Weapons America Used to Strike Iran — and Shield Against Retaliation |work=[[Business Insider]] |first=Jake |last=Epstein |date=28 February 2026 |access-date=28 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Bozorgmehr |first1=Najmeh |last2=Ghaffari |first2=Bita |date=28 February 2026 |title=Tehran Started Its Working Week. Then Came the Explosions |url=https://www.ft.com/content/97db4b54-ebd6-4210-8f66-6917f157823a |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[Financial Times]]}}</ref> The strikes took place during negotiations over Iran's nuclear program,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Live Updates: U.S. And Israel Attack Iran |url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/live-updates-u-s-and-israel-attack-iran |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=[[PBS News]] |language=en-us |quote=The strikes opened a stunning new chapter in U.S. intervention in Iran, marking the second time in eight months that the Trump administration has attacked the country during talks over its nuclear program.}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Iran's Foreign Minister Says He's Unsure Why U.S. Attacked During Nuclear Talks |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/iran-attack-us-israel-regime-change-trump-netanyahu-araghchi-rcna261124 |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=[[NBC News]] |language=en}}</ref> and coincided with the holy month of [[Ramadan]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.stern.de/politik/ausland/iran--angriff-mitten-im-ramadan---war-das-absicht--das-sagt-ein-experte-37190302.html |title=Iran: Angriff Mitten Im Ramadan – War Das Absicht? Das Sagt Ein Experte |language=de |trans-title=Iran: Attack in the middle of Ramadan – was it intentional? An expert weighs in |date=5 March 2026 |magazine=[[Stern (magazine)|Stern]] |access-date=14 March 2026 |archive-date=5 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260305165328/https://www.stern.de/politik/ausland/iran--angriff-mitten-im-ramadan---war-das-absicht--das-sagt-ein-experte-37190302.html |url-status=live}}</ref> The operation was codenamed Operation Roaring Lion{{efn|{{langx|he|מִבְצַע שְׁאָגַת הָאֲרִי|Mivtsá She'agát Ha'arí|engvar=ox}}, {{IPA|he|mivˈt͡sä ʃe̞.äˈɡätʰ hä.ʔäˈʁi|pron|small=yes}}}} by Israel.<ref name="cnn-roaringlion">{{#invoke:cite |news |first=Tal |last=Shalev |date=28 February 2026 |title=Israel Names Operation Against Iran "Roaring Lion" |url=https://www.cnn.com/world/live-news/israel-iran-attack-02-28-26-hnk-intl?post-id=cmm60zpmz001v3b6pkd1t046n |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name="ynet-lion">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Munitz |first=Shmuel |date=6 March 2026 |title=From Ancient Israel to Modern Iran: The Enduring Symbolism of the Lion |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/culture/article/sk0ujovk11l |access-date=18 March 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref> The [[Israeli Air Force]] (IAF) said it struck 500 military targets in Iran in the largest combat sortie in its history.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Fabian |first=Emanuel |date=28 February 2026 |title=IDF Says 200 Jets Involved in Air Force's Largest-Ever Attack Sortie |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/idf-says-200-jets-involved-in-air-forces-largest-ever-attack-sortie/ |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref> Iranian naval vessels were also targeted.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Satellite Images Show Iranian Warship Burning After US Israel Strikes |date=28 February 2026 |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/satellite-images-show-iranian-warship-burning-after-us-israel-strikes-2026-2 |work=[[Business Insider]] |access-date=1 March 2026}}</ref> Israel said it used over 1,200&nbsp;bombs in 24&nbsp;hours.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Israel Claims to Have Dropped over 1,200 Bombs on Iran in One Day |url=https://aje.news/p4rw7y?update=4349719 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |access-date=1 March 2026 |language=en}}</ref> US{{nbsp}}strikes were carried out by planes based around the Middle East and from aircraft carriers.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Update from Eric Schmitt |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/02/28/world/iran-strikes-trump/5df7d9a6-2d1a-577e-9c63-d40948472442 |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

[[File:Operation-Roaring-Lion-0017.jpg|thumb|[[General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon|F-16]] fighter jets of the [[Israeli Air Force|IAF]] over [[Deir ez-Zor]], [[Syria]] during Operation Roaring Lion.]]
Initial strikes killed Iran's supreme leader Ali Khamenei and [[List of Iranian officials killed during the 2026 Iran war|other top Iranian officials]],<ref name="AP timeline">{{cite news |last1=Anna |first1=Cara |title=A timeline of the Iran conflict and talks aimed at ending it |url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-timeline-trump-hormuz-war-ceasefire-04da58cbae991183f8b52ef5bf615963 |access-date=23 July 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=12 July 2026}}</ref> and hundreds of Iranians were killed or injured. The [[Iranian Red Crescent]] said 24 provinces were affected.<ref>{{cite news |title=Iranian Red Crescent says more than 200 killed in US-Israeli strikes |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/iranian-red-crescent-says-more-than-200-killed-in-us-israeli-strikes/ |access-date=23 July 2026 |work=[[Times of Israel]] |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]] |date=28 February 2026}}</ref> The strikes were coupled with cyberattacks on Iranian infrastructure, media, and phone apps, with messages calling on Iranians to rise up against their government.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Hackers Hit Iranian Apps, Websites After US-Israeli Strikes |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/hackers-hit-iranian-apps-websites-after-us-israeli-strikes-2026-03-01/ |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref><ref name = "JPost hack">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Gal |first=Itai |date=28 February 2026 |title=Israel Plunges Iran into Darkness with Largest Cyberattack in History During Attack Against Iran |url=https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/defense-news/article-888271 |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Israel Hacked Popular Iranian Prayer App to Urge Defections, Resistance |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-strikes-2026/card/israel-hacked-popular-iranian-prayer-app-to-urge-defections-resistance-wtYyb29CmKrTXoJBIV3C |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]]}}</ref> The cyberattacks resulted in a near-total internet blackout in Iran, lasting over 60{{nbsp}}hours with connectivity dropping to as low as 1%{{nbsp}}of normal levels, disrupting government communications, state media, and public services.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=The Digital Front: Iran's Internet Down for Second Day Amid Reports of U.S.-Israel Cyberattacks |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/02/irans-internet-down-amid-reports-of-us-israel-cyberattacks.html |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[CNBC]]}}</ref><ref name = "JPost hack"/> [[2026 Internet blackout in Iran|Iran restricted internet access]], allowing access only to government-approved users until 26 May.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Davies |first1=Maia |last2=Habibiazad |first2=Ghoncheh |title=Internet starts coming back in Iran after months-long blackout |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1w22y1n74do |access-date=23 July 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |date=26 May 2026}}</ref>

Israeli officials said months-long planning preceded the strikes, allowing them to pinpoint targets, attain "tactical surprise", and gain US support.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Israel Says Months of Planning Led to Surprise Iran Strikes |date=28 February 2026 |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202602286942 |website=[[Iran International]] |publisher=Volant Media UK Ltd |access-date=28 February 2026}}</ref> Attacking during the morning, rather than at night when most of Israel's previous attacks on Iran took place, added to the element of surprise.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Halbfinger |first1=David M. |last2=Bergman |first2=Ronen |location=Jerusalem, Tel Aviv |title=How the Assault on Iran Unfolded |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/01/world/middleeast/iran-israel-strikes.html |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=1 March 2026}}</ref> Israel declared a state of emergency, citing expectation of Iranian retaliation, and warned its citizens to remain in protected areas.<ref name="Liebermann-2026">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Liebermann |first=Oren |date=28 February 2026 |title=Israel Launches Strike Against Iran, Declares State of Emergency Across Country |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/28/middleeast/israel-attack-iran-intl-hnk?post-id=cmm5xzk1y00003b6pin7tql07 |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |first1=Edna |last1=Mohamed |first2=Federica |last2=Marsi |date=28 February 2026 |title=Israel Attacks Iran |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/2/28/live-israel-launches-attacks-on-iran-multiple-explosions-heard-in-tehran |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> Israel called up 20,000 reservists in addition to the 50,000 on duty.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/israel-calls-up-20000-reservists-in-addition-to-the-50000-reservists-currently-on-duty/ |title=Israel Calls up 20,000 Reservists, In Addition to the 50,000 Reservists Currently on Duty |first=Emanuel |last=Fabian |date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]]}}</ref> The [[Israeli Ministry of Health]] moved its hospital operations underground.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Yosef |first=Eugenia |date=28 February 2026 |title=Israeli Hospitals Shift Underground as Health Ministry Orders Highest Readiness Level |url=https://www.cnn.com/world/live-news/israel-iran-attack-02-28-26-hnk-intl?post-id=cmm5zx2ic00003b6rvnargvaq |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref>

On 28{{nbsp}}February, Trump released a statement saying the purpose of the strikes was [[regime change]], citing Iran's support for non-state actors such as [[Hamas]] and [[Hezbollah]], [[Human rights in Iran|killings of protesters]], chants of "[[Death to America]]", and alleged history of attacking US civilians and soldiers, as well as the [[Iran hostage crisis]].<ref name="CBS Major-Combat-Operations"/> Trump and [[Benjamin Netanyahu]] warned of the potential threat of nuclear weapons in Iran and called on Iranians to overthrow their government.<ref name="CBS Major-Combat-Operations">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Trump Announces "Major Combat Operations" in Iran. Watch the Full Video and Read His Statement. |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-full-statement-on-us-iran-attack-major-combat-operations/ |work=[[CBS News]] |access-date=28 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Netanyahu Says Israel, US Launched Strikes to 'Remove the Existential Threat' Posed by Iran |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/netanyahu-says-israel-us-launched-strikes-to-remove-the-existential-threat-posed-by-iran/ |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref> Israeli defense minister [[Israel Katz]] labeled the strikes a "pre-emptive attack" intended to "remove threats to...Israel".<ref name="Liebermann-2026"/> Iran denied that it intended to attack the US.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Scahill |first=Jeremy |date=3 March 2026 |title=Exclusive: Iran's Deputy Foreign Minister Rejects Trump's 'Big Lie' About Why He Went to War |url=https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/exclusive-interview-iran-deputy-foreign-minister-esmail-baghaei-trump-israel-big-lie |access-date=5 March 2026 |website=[[Drop Site News]]}}</ref>

[[File:US bases in the Middle East.svg|thumb|Major [[List of American military installations|US military bases and installations]] in the Middle East, including bases used during the strikes]]
Iranian units reacted within hours by launching missiles and drones. Iran codenamed its response {{vanchor|Operation True Promise IV}},{{efn|Previously, Iran had launched [[Operation True Promise I|I]], [[Operation True Promise II|II]], and [[Operation True Promise III|III]] on a more limited scale.}}{{efn|{{langx|fa|عملیات وعده صادق ۴|Amaliyat-e Va'deh-ye Sadegh 4}}}} and state media dubbed the events the Ramadan War.{{efn|{{langx|fa|جنگ رمضان|Jang-e Ramazān}}}}<ref name="arabnews-eid">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=20 March 2026 |title=Iran to Mark Eid Al-Fitr On Saturday: State TV |url=https://www.arabnews.com/node/2636982/middle-east |access-date=20 March 2026 |work=[[Arab News]] |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]]}}</ref> Iran struck Israeli targets in [[Tel Aviv]] and [[Haifa]]<ref name="BBC Tehran response">{{#invoke:cite |news |script-title=fa:جنگ آمریکا و اسرائیل با ایران؛ چرا واکنش تهران این‌بار تنها چند ساعت طول کشید؟ |trans-title=The war between the U.S. and Israel with Iran; why did Tehran's response this time only last a few hours? |url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/articles/ce94dk4yy2eo |work=[[BBC News]] Persian |date=28 February 2026 |language=fa |access-date=1 March 2026}}</ref> as well as countries throughout the Persian Gulf.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=28 February 2026 |title=Iran Targets US Bases Across Persian Gulf States, IRGC-Aligned Outlet Says |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202602282948 |access-date=28 February 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> Targets included Bahrain's capital [[Manama]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Lehmann |first=Noam |date=28 February 2026 |title=Bahrain: Sirens Activated as Iran Targets US Bases |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/bahrain-sirens-activated-as-iran-targets-us-bases/ |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Yee |first1=Isaac |last2=Rebane |first2=Teele |date=28 February 2026 |title=Videos Show Smoke Rising Near US Navy Facility in Bahrain |url=https://www.cnn.com/world/live-news/israel-iran-attack-02-28-26-hnk-intl?post-id=cmm64k1hv00003b6rj8g5hm4u |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Kuwait International Airport]], the United Arab Emirates' capital [[Abu Dhabi]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Explosions Reported in Kuwait and UAE |url=https://news.am/eng/news/932924.html |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=Armenia News |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=28 February 2026 |title=Drone Attacks Targets Kuwait International Airport |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202602283083 |access-date=28 February 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Riyadh]] and [[Eastern Province, Saudi Arabia|Eastern Province]] in Saudi Arabia,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Update from Ismaeel Naar |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/02/28/world/iran-strikes-trump/c23471fd-1ceb-5a75-93a8-a56a199d6b1f |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> and [[Erbil International Airport]] and the [[Consulate General of the United States in Erbil|US Consulate General in Erbil]] in Iraq.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=28 February 2026 |title=Drones Shot Down Over Erbil Near U.S. Consulate as Iran-Israel Conflict Expands to Iraqi Kurdistan |url=https://www.kurdistan24.net/en/story/896852/slug |access-date=28 February 2026 |website=[[Kurdistan24]] |language=en}}</ref>

Among the first targets were radars, notably the American [[AN/FPS-132]] in Qatar, which degraded missile-warning capability in the region.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://militarywatchmagazine.com/article/iranian-strikes-destroyed-antimissile-radars|title=Iranian Strikes Have Destroyed $2.7 Billion Worth of High Value U.S. Anti-Missile Radars|website=Military Watch|date=8 March 2026}}</ref> Iran reported striking the US bases of [[Al Udeid Air Base]] in Qatar, [[Ali Al Salem Air Base]] in Kuwait,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://france24.com/en/middle-east/20260228-what-we-know-about-us-military-bases-mideast-gulf-targeted-iran-retaliatory-strikes |title=Iran Targets US Military Bases in the Middle East with Retaliatory Strikes |date=28 February 2026 |work=[[France 24]] |access-date=4 March 2026}}</ref> [[Al Dhafra Air Base]] in the UAE, and the [[US Fifth Fleet]] headquarters in Bahrain.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Salem |first=Mostafa |date=28 February 2026 |title=Iran's IRGC Targeted Four US Bases in the Middle East, Iranian Media Reports |url=https://www.cnn.com/world/live-news/israel-iran-attack-02-28-26-hnk-intl?post-id=cmm64boa9000m356rh4can18y |access-date=28 February 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref>  On 1 or 2 March, Iran struck the radar bases for US [[Terminal High Altitude Area Defense|THAAD]] missile defense systems in Jordan, the UAE and Saudi Arabia, destroying at least one.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last1=Bordeaux |first1=Thomas |last2=Mezzofiore |first2=Gianluca |date=5 March 2026 |title=Radar Bases Housing Key US Missile Interceptor Hit in Jordan and UAE, Satellite Images Show |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/05/middleeast/radar-bases-us-missile-defense-iran-war-intl-invs |access-date=26 March 2026 |website=CNN |language=en}}</ref> On 1 March, Iran launched more strikes,<ref name="Reuters-2026">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=More Strikes Aimed at Iran After Khamenei's Death, Trump Issues New Warning |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/more-strikes-aimed-iran-after-us-israeli-assault-kills-supreme-leader-2026-03-01/ |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> including missiles and drones on Bahrain, Israel, Jordan, Kuwait, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, and the UAE.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Gambrell |first1=Jon |last2=Lidman |first2=Melanie |last3=Boak |first3=Josh |first4=Eric |last4=Tucker |date=1 March 2026 |title=Iran Fires Missiles at Israel and Gulf States After US-Israeli Strike Kills Khamenei |url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-israel-us-03-01-2026-693bc30bbbc98660d81f4a13f65ca10f |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Christou |first1=William |last2=Giuffrida |first2=Angela |date=1 March 2026 |title=Explosions Rock Dubai, Bahrain, Jordan and Kuwait as War Spreads Across Middle East |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/28/dubais-famous-fairmont-hotel-in-flames-after-iranian-air-strike |access-date=2 April 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> The UK reported "missiles fired in the direction of Cyprus", but "don't believe they were targeted at Cyprus". However, the presidents of Cyprus and [[Northern Cyprus]] contradicted the claims that any missiles were fired at Cyprus.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Two Iranian Missiles Fired in Direction of Cyprus: British Defence Secretary |url=https://aje.news/p4rw7y?update=4350207 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |access-date=1 March 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Iran Launched Missiles at Cyprus, Threatening Thousands of British Troops Stationed There |url=https://www.jpost.com/international/article-888356 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |access-date=1 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Maddox |first=David |date=1 March 2026 |title=Iran Missiles Fired Towards UK Military Bases in Cyprus, Defence Minister Says |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/politics/iran-missiles-cyprus-defence-secretary-b2929655.html |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]]}}</ref> {{anchor|MKD VYOM}} The [[Palau]]-flagged ''Skylight'' and [[Marshall Islands]]-flagged ''MKD VYOM'' tankers were targeted off Oman's coast.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Hand |first=Marcus |date=1 March 2026 |title=Ships Avoid the Strait of Hormuz, Tanker Hit off Oman |url=https://www.seatrade-maritime.com/security/ships-avoid-the-strait-of-hormuz-tanker-hit-off-oman |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=SeatradeMaritime}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Saba |first=Yousef |date=1 March 2026 |title=Three Tankers Damaged in Gulf and One Seafarer Killed as US-Iran Conflict Escalates |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/three-tankers-damaged-gulf-us-iran-conflict-escalates-2026-03-01/ |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Seafarer Death Confirmed Aboard Product Tanker Struck off Oman |url=https://www.shipmanagementinternational.com/news/c4w2gfpy7n4paz9-tpat6-3k6xt-xt6kh-538b8-ye8r7-3gltm-9bm6d-zbm53-xm5am-jwn7b-97hlw-7c2ns-z9rmx |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=Ship Management International}}</ref> Shipping through the Strait of Hormuz slowed to a standstill,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Wells |first1=Peter |last2=Thomas |first2=Nathalie |last3=Wheatley |first3=Jonathan |last4=Ralph |first4=Oliver |last5=Munir |first5=Zehra |last6=Meixler |first6=Eli |last7=Cash |first7=Kieran |last8=Ryan |first8=Orla |last9=Vickers |first9=Julian |date=1 March 2026 |title=Middle East War Day 2 as It Happened: Oil Flows Through Strait of Hormuz Dry Up, Opec+ Plans to Raise Output |url=https://www.ft.com/content/e026b4a7-1115-493a-9b31-c8b0b5965491 |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Financial Times]]}}</ref> with 150 freight ships, including oil tankers, stalled.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Nahost-Liveblog: ++ Mehrere Tote Bei Raketeneinschlag in Israel ++ |url=https://www.tagesschau.de/newsticker/liveblog-israel-usa-angriffe-iran-102.html |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[Tagesschau (German TV programme)|Tagesschau]] |language=de |trans-title=Middle East Liveblog: ++ Several dead in rocket strike in Israel ++}}</ref>

British prime minister [[Keir Starmer]] said the US could use British bases for "defensive" strikes on Iran<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=US Can Use UK Bases for Missile Strikes on Iran: Starmer |url=https://www.euractiv.com/news/us-can-use-uk-bases-for-missile-strikes-on-iran-starmer/ |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]] |work=[[Euractiv]] |access-date=1 March 2026 |date=1 March 2026}}</ref> and disclosed that Ukrainian and other specialists would aid Gulf efforts to foil Iranian drone strikes.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |author1=Guardian staff |title=Ukraine War Briefing: Starmer Says Ukrainian Experts Will Help Shoot Down Iranian Drone Attacks in Gulf |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/02/ukraine-war-briefing-drone-experts-to-stop-iran-drone-attacks-starmer |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=3 March 2026 |date=2 March 2026 |quote=And we will also bring experts from Ukraine, together with our own experts, to help Gulf partners shoot down Iranian drones attacking them.}}</ref> Saudi Crown Prince Salman, with US backing, vowed to employ military force against Iranian incursions, calling Iranian strikes "cowardly" due to Saudi airspace being closed to US and Israeli attackers.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Saudi Arabia Authorizes Retaliation Against Iran, CNN |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603010896 |website=[[Iran International]] |access-date=1 March 2026 |date=1 March 2026}}</ref> Trump announced that the US had accepted an Iranian proposal to negotiations.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Scherer |first=Michael |date=1 March 2026 |title='I Have Agreed to Talk' |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/national-security/2026/03/trump-iran-attack-negotiations/686201/ |magazine=[[The Atlantic]] |access-date=1 March 2026 |archive-date=1 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260301183214/https://www.theatlantic.com/national-security/2026/03/trump-iran-attack-negotiations/686201/ |url-status=live}}</ref> However, Ali Larijani ruled out talks.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://abc7news.com/live-updates/iran-live-updates-trump-says-major-combat-operations-have-begun/18660347/entry/18666415 |title='We Will Not Negotiate with the United States,' Iranian Official Says |date=1 March 2026 |work=[[KABC-TV]] |access-date=4 March 2026}}</ref>

[[File:Epic Fury Strike compilation (997855).webm|thumb|2 March: Montage of [[US Central Command]] strikes]]

On 2 March, the [[US embassy in Kuwait]] was struck and closed indefinitely.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-us-war-day-3-american-deaths-israel-gulf-allies-hit-missile-strikes/ |title=Live Updates: U.S. Death Toll in Iran War Rises to 6 as Trump Says Campaign Could Last 5 Weeks |first=Tucker |last=Reals |date=3 March 2026 |work=[[CBS News]]}}</ref><ref name="Reals"/> The US-flagged tanker ''Stena Imperative'' and the Honduras-flagged tanker ''Athe Nova'' were struck.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=US Flagged Products Tanker Hit by Unknown Projectiles in Bahrain Port, Sources Say |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-flagged-products-tanker-hit-by-unknown-projectiles-bahrain-port-sources-say-2026-03-02/ |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> An advisor to an IRGC commander said he would set fire to any ship coming through the Strait of Hormuz, and added that no oil will leave the area.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=McCreesh |first1=Shawn |last2=Pager |first2=Tyler |last3=Schmitt |first3=Eric |last4=Cooper |first4=Helene |last5=Pérez-Peña |first5=Richard |title=Live Updates: Trump Suggests Extended War on Iran as U.S. Adds to Forces in Mideast |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/02/world/iran-us-israel-attack-trump |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=2 March 2026}}</ref>

Qatar claimed that it had shot down two [[Sukhoi Su-24|Iranian Su-24{{nbsp}}bombers]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Salem |first1=Mostafa |last2=Kent |first2=Lauren |date=2 March 2026 |title=Qatar Says It Shot Down Two Iranian Bomber Aircraft |url=https://edition.cnn.com/world/live-news/iran-israel-us-attack-03-02-26-intl-hnk?post-id=cmm9dkjpf00003b6ps4g5qwvo |access-date=14 March 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref> The Qatari Ministry of Defense announced that [[Ras Laffan Industrial City]], the main Qatari gas facility, and [[Mesaieed Industrial Area]] were struck by Iranian drones.<ref name="bloomberg4march">{{#invoke:cite |web |last1=Stapczynski |first1=Stephen |last2=Liao |first2=Ruth |last3=El Wardany |first3=Salma |date=4 March 2026 |title=Qatar's Hard-Won Reputation as Safest Gas Supplier Lost in Days |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-03-04/iran-war-dents-qatar-s-reputation-as-lng-s-safest-bet |website=[[Bloomberg News]]}}</ref> According to satellite imagery analysis by the Energy Economics and Society Research Institute, Ras Laffan appeared to not have been damaged before the "unprecedented shutdown" which sent fuel prices higher.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=7 March 2026 |last1=Liao |first1=Ruth |last2=Stapczynski |first2=Stephen |title=Qatar's Main LNG Equipment Intact, Satellite Analysis Shows |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-03-06/qatar-s-main-lng-equipment-intact-satellite-analysis-shows |website=[[Bloomberg News]]}}</ref>

[[File:Attack on Sanandaj Residential Areas 1.jpg|thumb|2 March: Damage to residential buildings in [[Sanandaj]], Iranian Kurdistan]]
The US and Israel attacked the [[Natanz Nuclear Facility]]<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Iran Says Natanz Nuclear Site Hit in US-Israeli Strikes |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/china/iran-says-natanz-nuclear-site-hit-us-israeli-strikes-2026-03-02/? |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> and the Iranian media reported damage to the Khatam-al-Anbia and Gandhi hospitals.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/articles/cy4wxk7e71xo |script-title=fa:حملات گسترده هوایی به پایتخت ایران؛ آسیب‌ به بیمارستان‌های گاندی و خاتم‌الانبیاء در تهران |title= |date=1 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News Persian]] |language=fa |access-date=2 March 2026 |trans-title=Massive airstrikes on Iran's capital; damage to Gandhi and Khatam al-Anbiya hospitals in Tehran}}</ref> In a [[friendly fire]] incident, the pilot of an [[F/A-18]] of the [[Kuwait Air Force]] shot down three US [[F-15E]]{{nbsp}}fighters.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 March 2026 |title=Kuwait Shoots Down US Jets: All About F/A-18 Hornet That Accidentally Shot Down F-15s Amid Iran Tensions |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/kuwait-shoots-down-us-jets-all-about-f-a-18-hornet-that-shot-down-mcdonnell-douglas-f-15s-amid-iran-tensions-101772592785736.html |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[Hindustan Times]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Seligman |first1=Lara |last2=Weisgerber |first2=Marcus |last3=Holliday |first3=Shelby |date=4 March 2026 |title=Exclusive: Kuwaiti Jet Fighter Mistakenly Downed U.S. F-15s, Initial Reports Say |url=https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/kuwaiti-jet-fighter-mistakenly-downed-u-s-f-15s-initial-reports-say-4ab64e56 |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |script-title=fa:سنتکام: سقوط سه اف-۱۵اشتباه پدافند کویت بود؛ قرارگاه خاتم‌الانبیاء: ما زدیم |title= |trans-title=CentCom: The downing of three F-15s was a mistake by Kuwaiti defense; Khatam al-Anbiya base: We hit |url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/articles/ckg1xz7pldgo |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News Persian]] |language=fa}}</ref><ref name="Reals">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Reals |first=Tucker |date=2 March 2026 |title=Live Updates: U.S. Military Confirms 4 Troops Killed in Iran War; Kuwait Downs 3 U.S. Jets in 'Friendly Fire' |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-us-war-day-3-american-deaths-israel-gulf-allies-hit-missile-strikes/ |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[CBS News]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Israel and Hezbollah exchanged strikes.<ref name="Kleinbaum-2026"/> Hezbollah began firing rockets and missiles on Israel in retaliation for the killing of Khamenei.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=3 March 2026 |title=Israel Strikes Beirut, Lebanon State Media Says Hamas Official Killed |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260303-hezbollah-says-targeted-3-israeli-bases-after-strikes-on-lebanon |access-date=6 March 2026 |work=[[France 24]] |language=en}}</ref> Hezbollah claimed that the attack was a "defensive act" after more than a year of Israeli [[Hezbollah–Israel conflict (2023–present)|attacks]] despite [[2024 Israel–Lebanon ceasefire agreement|a 2024 truce]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Hezbollah Claims Attack on Israel Was 'Defensive Act' After Year of Israeli Strikes |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/hezbollah-claims-attack-on-israel-was-defensive-act-after-year-of-israeli-strikes/ |access-date=25 April 2026 |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]] |work=[[The Times of Israel]]}}</ref> It added that it restarted fighting to force Israel to stop its aggression and evacuate from [[Israeli–Lebanese conflict|seized Lebanese territories]], emphasizing that the move was unrelated to the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=5 March 2026 |title=Hezbollah Leader: Resumed Fighting with Israel Not Linked to War on Iran |url=https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2026/03/04/lebanon-hezbollah-leader-israel-aggression/6851772658355/ |website=[[United Press International]]}}</ref>

Lebanon banned military activities by Hezbollah after the attacks.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=Lebanon's Ban on Hezbollah 'Activities': Bold but Difficult to Implement |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/3/3/lebanons-ban-on-hezbollah-activities-bold-but-difficult-to-implement |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref> An IDF spokesperson stated the attack was "an official declaration of war by Hezbollah", vowing to "neutralize" the threat.<ref name="Kleinbaum-2026">{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Kleinbaum |first=Yair |date=1 March 2026 |title=Breaking: Hezbollah Officially Declared War on Israel |url=https://www.jfeed.com/news/tb8tr7 |access-date=1 March 2026 |website=JFeed |language=en}}</ref> Israel struck [[southern Lebanon]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Kraus |first1=Yair |last2=Glikman |first2=Eitan |last3=Shashua |first3=Itamar |date=1 March 2026 |title=Israel Strikes Southern Lebanon and Tehran as Hezbollah Joins Iran War |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bj5jpbmfbl |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |first1=Joseph |last1=Stepansky |first2=Zaid |last2=Sabah |title=US, Israel Attack Iran Live: Trump Vows to Avenge 3 American Soldiers |date=2 March 2026 |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/2/us-israel-attack-iran-live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302010612/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/2/us-israel-attack-iran-live |archive-date=2 March 2026 |access-date=2 March 2026 |url-status=deviated |website=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Iran, Le News Dalla Guerra. Missili Di Hezbollah Dal Libano Verso Haifa, Israele Risponde. Teheran Sotto Attacco dell'Idf |url=https://www.repubblica.it/esteri/2026/03/02/diretta/iran_guerra_usa_israele_news_oggi-425194152/ |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[la Repubblica]] |language=it |trans-title=Iran, news from the war. Hezbollah launches missiles from Lebanon toward Haifa, Israel responds. Tehran under attack from the IDF}}</ref> Beirut, and the [[Beqaa Valley]],<ref name="Kleinbaum-2026"/> with the IDF saying it had killed the head of Hezbollah's intelligence Hussein Makled<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Fabian |first=Emanuel |date=2 March 2026 |title=IDF Says It Killed Hezbollah Intelligence Chief in Overnight Strike |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/idf-says-it-killed-hezbollah-intelligence-chief-in-overnight-strike/ |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Israeli Military Says It Killed Head of Hezbollah's Intelligence Headquarters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-military-says-it-killed-head-hezbollahs-intelligence-headquarters-2026-03-02/ |work=[[Reuters]] |date=2 March 2026 |access-date=2 March 2026}}</ref> and Adham Adnan al-Othman, the head of [[Palestinian Islamic Jihad]]'s armed wing, the [[Al-Quds Brigades]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Palestinian Islamic Jihad Armed Wing Says Lebanon Commander Killed in Israeli Strikes |url=https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1496991/palestinian-islamic-jihad-armed-wing-says-lebanon-commander-killed-in-israeli-strikes.html |access-date=11 March 2026 |work=[[L'Orient Today]] |language=en}}</ref> The Royal Air Force station at [[RAF Akrotiri|Akrotiri]], Cyprus, was targeted by a drone strike causing damage to a runway.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=RAF Responding to Suspected Drone Strike at UK Base in Cyprus, MoD Says |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn5ge95q6y7t?post=asset%3Ab765c35c-353a-49db-9fe9-8e35d0214492#post |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Cleaver |first=Tom |date=1 March 2026 |title=UK Cyprus Base Hit by Drone |url=https://cyprus-mail.com/2026/03/02/security-threat-declared-at-uk-cyprus-bases |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[Cyprus Mail]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Smith |first=Helena |date=2 March 2026 |title=Authorities in Cyprus Have Confirmed the Drone Strike |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/mar/01/us-israel-war-on-iran-ayatollah-ali-khamenei-i-dead-latest-reports?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-69a4d4488f080cbafb286774#block-69a4d4488f080cbafb286774 |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Sabbagh |first1=Dan |title=Hezbollah Said to Have Launched Drone That Struck UK RAF Airbase in Cyprus |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/02/uk-airbase-raf-akrotiri-cyprus-suspected-drone-strike |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=3 March 2026 |date=2 March 2026}}</ref> Another strike on Cyprus led to Greece announcing that it would deploy frigates and [[F-16]]s to defend Cyprus from strikes by Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Greece Deploys Frigates and F-16s To Cyprus Amid Rising Security Tensions |url=https://www.ekathimerini.com/politics/foreign-policy/1296727/greece-deploys-frigates-and-f-16s-to-cyprus-amid-rising-security-tensions/ |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[Kathimerini]] |language=en}}</ref> The pro-Iran militant group [[Iraqi Guardians of Blood Brigades]] claimed responsibility for attacks on the US [[Victory Base Complex|Victory Base]] near [[Baghdad International Airport]] and [[Erbil]] in the [[Kurdistan Region]] of Iraq.<ref>{{#invoke:Cite|web|first1=Joseph|last1=Stepansky|first2=Zaid|last2=Sabah|title=US, Israel attack Iran live: Trump vows to avenge 3 American soldiers|date=2 March 2026|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/2/us-israel-attack-iran-live|access-date=28 February 2026|website=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Explosions Rock Iraq's Erbil |url=https://aje.news/wwomw4?update=4354362 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |access-date=2 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Iranian Attack Sets off Fire Near Bahrain's Mina Salman Port |url=https://aje.news/wwomw4?update=4353493 |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref> The [[Islamic Resistance in Iraq]] claimed responsibility for 23{{nbsp}}drone strikes on US{{nbsp}}assets in Erbil.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Iran-Aligned Group Claims 23 Drone Attacks on US Sites in Erbil |url=https://aje.news/wwomw4?update=4356034 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref>

