On 3 March, US and Israeli strikes destroyed the SNSC headquarters,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Israel Strikes Iran Leadership Compound in Central Tehran |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603031120 |website=[[Iran International]] |access-date=3 March 2026 |date=3 March 2026}}</ref> the [[Expediency Discernment Council]] building in Tehran,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Video Shows Ruins of Iran's Expediency Council Building After Strikes |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603037480 |website=[[Iran International]] |access-date=3 March 2026 |date=3 March 2026}}</ref> and what Israeli officials described as an alleged underground nuclear weapons facility called Min Zadai.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=IDF Destroys Secret Nuclear Site, Thousands of Missile Pads |url=https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-888715 |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en}}</ref> The proximity of these strikes to the [[Bushehr Nuclear Power Plant]] (about {{cvt|12|km}} away) prompted the Russian agency [[Rosatom]] to suspend construction on new units and evacuate non-essential staff.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Civilian Iran Air Passenger Jet Destroyed at Bushehr Airport, Rosatom Nuclear Plant Suspended |url=https://sundayguardianlive.com/world/iran-israel-latest-news-civilian-iran-air-passenger-jet-destroyed-at-bushehr-airport-rosatom-nuclear-plant-suspended-173844/amp/ |work=[[The Sunday Guardian]] |access-date=4 March 2026 |date=3 March 2026}}</ref> A CIA site in US embassy in Riyadh was hit by Iranian drones.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/iran-strikes-cia-facilities-prompt-questions-about-possible-russian-role-2026-07-22/|title=Iran strikes on CIA facilities prompt questions about possible Russian role|website=[[Reuters]]|date=22 July 2026}}</ref> US officials said its forces had severely damaged Iran's naval capabilities, mainly in the [[Gulf of Oman]], where several Iranian warships were destroyed and key bases hit.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Ozberk |first=Tayfun |date=2 March 2026 |title=US Strikes Destroy Iran's Main Naval Assets |url=https://www.navalnews.com/naval-news/2026/03/us-strikes-destroy-irans-main-naval-assets/ |access-date=3 March 2026 |website=Naval News |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last1=Trevithick |first1=Joseph |last2=Rogoway |first2=Tyler |date=2 March 2026 |title=Iran's Key Naval Base On Strait Of Hormuz Set Ablaze From Strikes |url=https://www.twz.com/news-features/irans-key-naval-base-on-strait-of-hormuz-set-ablaze-from-strikes |access-date=3 March 2026 |website=The War Zone |language=en-US}}</ref> Debris from an airstrike damaged [[Golestan Palace]], a [[UNESCO World Heritage Site]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=UNESCO Shares Concerns over Protection of Cultural Heritage Sites |url=https://www.euronews.com/culture/2026/03/03/unesco-expresses-concern-over-the-protection-of-cultural-heritage-sites-in-middle-east |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[Euronews]] |language=en}}</ref> causing UNESCO to issue a statement that damaging UNESCO sites is against international law.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Purwar |first=Krati |date=3 March 2026 |title=How Iran Conflict Damaged Golestan Palace, Once Home Of Peacock Throne Looted From Delhi |url=https://www.ndtv.com/lifestyle/how-iran-conflict-damaged-golestan-palace-once-home-of-peacock-throne-looted-from-delhi-11162756/amp/1 |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[NDTV]]}}</ref> Israel Katz authorized a [[2026 Lebanon war|ground invasion of Lebanon]] on 3 March with forces from the [[91st Division (Israel)|91st Division]], with the stated goal to establish a "security layer" against Hezbollah. The [[Lebanese government]] reported that Israeli attacks reached [[Kfarkela]] and [[Al-Qaouzah|Qouzah]], leading the [[Lebanese army]] to redeploy from newly established border posts.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Israel Launches Ground Incursion in Lebanon as Hezbollah Targets Military Bases |url=https://www.palestinechronicle.com/israel-launches-ground-incursion-in-lebanon-as-hezbollah-targets-military-bases/ |website=The Palestine Chronicle |access-date=4 March 2026 |date=3 March 2026}}</ref> Israel reported that it killed [[Daoud Alizadeh]], the commander of the Quds Force's Lebanon branch, in Tehran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Fabian |first=Emanuel |date=3 March 2026 |title=Top IRGC Commander, Responsible for Lebanon, Killed in Tehran Strike — IDF |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/top-irgc-commander-responsible-for-lebanon-killed-in-tehran-strike-idf/ |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref>

[[File:Attack on residential homes in central Tehran 1.jpg|thumb|4 March: Buildings in Tehran damaged by US–Israeli strikes]]
Western diplomats said Qatar had struck Iran after Iran had attempted to strike Doha's airport and Qatar shot down two Iranian [[Su-24]] bombers.<ref name="wsj3march">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=Trump Open to Supporting Armed Militias in Iran, U.S. Officials Say |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-israel-us-strikes-2026/card/trump-open-to-supporting-armed-militias-in-iran-u-s-officials-say-nydkWoLgSs641jEV68Dg |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Freiberg |first=Nava |date=3 March 2026 |title=Qatar Carried out Strikes in Iran, Saudi Arabia to Soon Follow — Israeli Reports |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/qatar-carried-out-strikes-in-iran-saudi-arabia-to-soon-follow-israeli-reports/ |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref> Qatar denied the accusation that it had joined the "campaign targeting Iran".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Qatar Denies Israeli Media Report That It's Carrying out Retaliatory Strikes in Iran |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/qatar-carried-out-strikes-in-iran-saudi-arabia-to-soon-follow-israeli-reports/ |date=3 March 2026 |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]]}}</ref> Iran warned it would hit all economic hubs in the Middle East,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=Iran Says Will Hit All Mideast Economic Hubs If US-Israeli Attacks Persist |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/defence/iran-says-will-hit-all-mideast-economic-hubs-if-us-israeli-attacks-persist/articleshow/128981034.cms?from=mdr |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[The Economic Times]] |issn=0013-0389}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=3 March 2026 |title=Iran Says Will Hit All Mideast Economic Hubs If US-Israeli Attacks Persist |url=https://www.lbcgroup.tv/news/middleeastnews/909921/lbci-lebanon-articles/en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260303165117/https://www.lbcgroup.tv/news/middleeastnews/909921/lbci-lebanon-articles/en |archive-date=3 March 2026 |access-date=3 March 2026 |website=LBCIV7 |language=en}}</ref> and any defensive European military involvement would be considered an act of war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=Crisi Medio Oriente, L'Iran Minaccia l'Europa: Scatta L'allerta Militare E I Paesi Si Mobilitano |trans-title= |url=https://tg.la7.it/esteri/iran-minaccia-europa-allerta-militare-missili-03-03-2026-253543 |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[TGLA7]] |language=it}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Fouda |first1=Malek |title=Tehran Vows to Strike European Countries If They Join Iran War |url=https://www.euronews.com/2026/03/03/tehran-vows-to-strike-european-countries-if-they-join-iran-war |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[Euronews]] |date=3 March 2026 |language=en}}</ref>

On 4{{nbsp}}March, US secretary of state Marco Rubio announced that the US-Israeli attacks on Iran would increase in intensity.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=Iran Live Updates: US Embassies 'Under Direct Attack,' Rubio Says |url=https://abcnews.com/International/live-updates/iran-live-updates-israel-launches-preemptive-strike-iran/?id=130301492 |work=ABC News |language=en}}</ref> Israel attacks hit the [[Basij]] headquarters.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 March 2026 |title=Israel Says It Hits Security Headquarters Across Tehran, As Iran Attacks US Sites in Dubai and Qatar |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c62gg44d53xt |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> The IDF announced that an [[F-35I]] "Adir" shot down a Russian-made Iranian [[Yak-130]] fighter jet over Tehran, the first time that an F-35 has shot down a crewed fighter jet in air-to-air combat, and the first time the IAF shot down an aircraft since 1985.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/defense-news/article-888768 |title=Israel F-35 Downs Iranian Fighter Jet in First War Dogfight |date=5 March 2026 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]]}}</ref> Iran launched strikes against the [[Al Udeid Air Base]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 March 2026 |title=Qatar Says Al Udeid Air Base Hit by Ballistic Missile |url=https://abcnews.com/International/live-updates/iran-live-updates-israel-launches-preemptive-strike-iran/?id=130301492&entryId=130737063 |work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] |language=en}}</ref> and [[2026 Aramco refinery attack|Aramco's Ras Tanura]] oil refining facility.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 March 2026 |title=Saudi Aramco's Ras Tanura Struck Again by Unknown Projectile, Four Sources Say |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/saudi-aramcos-ras-tanura-struck-again-by-unknown-projectile-four-sources-say-2026-03-04/ |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> The US ordered the evacuation of non-essential workers in Cyprus in anticipation of Iranian strikes.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Papadopoulos |first=Kosta |date=4 March 2026 |title=America Evacuates Non-Essential Workers from Cyprus Greek City Times |url=https://greekcitytimes.com/2026/03/04/america-evacuates-non-essential-workers-from-cyprus/ |access-date=4 March 2026 |website=Greek City Times |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Chen |first=Eve |date=4 March 2026 |title=Reconsider Visiting This European Country, State Department Says |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/travel/2026/03/04/cyprus-travel-safety-risks/88978882007/ |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[USA Today]] |language=en-US}}</ref> A ballistic missile launched from Iran was intercepted by [[NATO]] air defense systems as it entered Turkish airspace, marking an escalation in the conflict.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 March 2026 |title=Turkey Says NATO Defences Destroyed Missile Fired from Iran over Mediterranean |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/turkey-says-nato-defences-destroyed-missile-fired-iran-over-mediterranean-2026-03-04/ |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> Turkey asserted its right to self-defense after the missile landed in [[Dörtyol]], [[Hatay Province]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 March 2026 |title=Turkey Says Iranian Ballistic Missile Entered Its Airspace, Shot Down by NATO |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/turkey-says-iranian-ballistic-missile-entered-its-airspace-shot-down-by-nato/ |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref> and NATO secretary general [[Mark Rutte]] stated that the alliance was committed to defending Turkey.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=5 March 2026 |title=Secretary General Mark Rutte Condemns Violation of Turkish Airspace |url=https://www.nato.int/cps/en/natohq/news_2026_03_05.htm |website=[[NATO]]}}</ref>

[[File:Indian Ocean Iranian vessel (998184).webm|thumb|4 March: {{USS|Charlotte|SSN-766|6}} [[Sinking of IRIS Dena|torpedoed]] [[IRIS Dena|IRIS{{nbsp}}''Dena'']]]]
An Iranian frigate, {{ship|IRIS|Dena}}, [[Sinking of IRIS Dena|was sunk]] in the Indian Ocean by [[United States Navy]] submarine {{USS|Charlotte|SSN-766|6}}, about {{convert|40|nmi}} south of [[Galle]], Sri Lanka. The vessel was returning to Iran following its participation in the [[International Fleet Review 2026]] and the multilateral [[Milan (naval exercise)|Exercise MILAN]] at [[Visakhapatnam]], India.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |agency=Agence France-Presse |date=4 March 2026 |title=Sri Lanka Rescues 32 Sailors from Sunk Iranian Warship |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/sri-lanka-rescues-sailors-from-sinking-iranian-ship/article70702468.ece |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[The Hindu]] |language=en-IN |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 March 2026 |title=Sri Lanka Sends Jets over Iran Naval Ship's Distress Call, Denies 'Submarine Attack' Reports |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/sri-lanka-navy-sends-ships-aircraft-after-distress-call-from-iranian-vessel-iris-dena-101772605277885.html |access-date=4 March 2026 |work=[[Hindustan Times]] |language=en}}</ref> The exercise required ships not to carry ammunition, and the US likely knew the ''Dena'' was defenseless, since it sent a maritime patrol aircraft to participate.<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=5 March 2026 |title=The Most Chilling Detail in the U.S. Attack on an Iranian Naval Ship |url=https://newrepublic.com/post/207429/us-attack-iran-naval-ship |access-date=6 March 2026 |magazine=[[The New Republic]] |issn=0028-6583}}</ref> It was the first ship sunk by a submarine in active combat since the [[Falklands War]], and the first by an American submarine since World War II.{{efn|name=Cheonan|In 2010, South Korean corvette {{ship|ROKS|Cheonan|PCC-772|6}} was [[ROKS Cheonan sinking|sunk]] near the border with North Korea. An investigation into the incident by a group of countries concluded that it was sunk by a [[torpedo]] launched by a North Korean [[Yono-class submarine|Yeono-class]] midget [[submarine]], though North Korea denied any responsibility.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://koreatimes.co.kr/www/news/nation/2010/04/205_64242.html |title=External Impact Likely Cause of Ship Sinking |work=[[The Korea Times]] |date=15 April 2010 |access-date=16 April 2010}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Asia-Pacific/2010/0520/North-Korea-rebuffs-South-Korea-s-evidence-on-Cheonan-attack/(page)/2 |title=North Korea Rebuffs South Korea's Evidence on ''Cheonan'' Attack |work=[[The Christian Science Monitor]] |date=20 May 2010 |access-date=1 June 2012}}</ref>}}<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |first1=Howard |last1=Altman |first2=Joseph |last2=Trevithick |date=4 March 2026 |title=U.S. Navy Submarine Torpedoes Iranian Frigate In Indian Ocean |url=https://www.twz.com/news-features/u-s-submarine-sinks-iranian-warship-in-the-indian-ocean |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=The War Zone |language=en-US |archive-date=4 March 2026 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20260304142650/https://www.twz.com/news-features/u-s-submarine-sinks-iranian-warship-in-the-indian-ocean |url-status=live}}</ref> 104 Iranians were killed.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Magee |first1=Caolán |last2=Kelliher |first2=Fiona |date=8 March 2026 |title='Projectile' Kills 2 in Saudi Arabia as Iran Attacks on the Gulf Continue |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/8/iran-live-israel-bombs-tehran-oil-depots-attacks-on-gulf-states-continue |access-date=8 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref>

The government of Azerbaijan said on 5 March that [[2026 alleged Iranian strikes on Azerbaijan|drones from Iran struck]] Azerbaijan's [[Nakhchivan exclave]]<ref name="Reuters-2026b">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=5 March 2026 |title=Missiles, Drones Coming from Iran Fell on Airport in Azerbaijan, Source Says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/missiles-drones-coming-iran-fell-airport-azerbaijan-source-says-2026-03-05/ |work=[[Reuters]] |access-date=5 March 2026}}</ref> damaging an airport and injuring two civilians.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=5 March 2026 |title=Azerbaijan MFA: Iran Carried out Drone Attack on Nakhchivan, Two Civilians Injured |url=https://en.apa.az/foreign-policy/azerbaijan-mfa-iran-carried-out-drone-attack-on-nakhchivan-two-civilians-injured-statement-494963 |access-date=5 March 2026 |website=[[Azerbaijani Press Agency]] |language=en}}</ref> Keir Starmer confirmed UK's bases on Cyprus would be used to defend the airspace of Jordan from Iranian drones,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Cleaver |first=Tom |date=3 March 2026 |title=Cyprus the Likely Launchpad as UK Jets Shoot Down Drones in Jordan |url=https://cyprus-mail.com/2026/03/03/cyprus-the-likely-launchpad-as-uk-jets-shoot-down-drones-in-jordan |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Cyprus Mail]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Cleaver |first=Tom |date=5 March 2026 |title=Starmer Confirms Use of Cyprus Base to Shoot Down Iranian Drones |url=https://cyprus-mail.com/2026/03/06/starmer-confirms-use-of-cyprus-base-to-shoot-down-iranian-drones |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Cyprus Mail]]}}</ref> while [[Italy]], the [[Netherlands]] and [[Spain]] confirmed they would send warships to defend Cyprus.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=5 March 2026 |title=Spain, Italy and Netherlands Join European Naval Deployment to Cyprus |url=https://www.euronews.com/2026/03/05/spain-italy-and-netherlands-join-european-naval-deployment-to-cyprus |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Euronews]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=5 March 2026 |title=Europe Commits to Expanding Iran Campaign as Israel Strikes Southern Lebanon |url=https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2026-03-05/europe-commits-to-expanding-iran-campaign-as-israel-strikes-southern-lebanon |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Los Angeles Times]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.agi.it/cronaca/news/2026-03-06/iran-fregata-martinengo-difesa-creta-35983530/ |title=La Fregata Martinengo Inviata a Difesa Di Cipro |trans-title=The frigate Martinengo sent to defend Cyprus |first=Davide |last=Sarsini |date=6 March 2026 |website=AGI |access-date=11 March 2026 |language=it}}</ref> [[Republic of Ireland|Ireland]] stated it was willing to protect Cyprus and join the European defense coalition mobilized around the island if requested.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=O'Keeffe |first=Cormac |date=5 March 2026 |title=Ireland Urged to Assist Cyprus If It Invokes EU Mutual Defence Clause |url=https://www.irishexaminer.com/news/arid-41804990.html |access-date=5 March 2026 |work=[[Irish Examiner]] |language=en}}</ref> The IDF killed Hamas official Wassim Attallah al-Ali in [[Beddawi]], Lebanon.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=5 March 2026 |title=Israel Strikes Beirut, Hamas Official Reportedly Killed |url=https://english.alarabiya.net/News/middle-east/2026/03/05/israel-strikes-beirut-lebanon-state-media-says-hamas-official-killed |access-date=11 March 2026 |work=[[Al Arabiya English]] |language=en}}</ref> Trump said on 6 March that there are "no time limits" for how long the war will continue.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=5 March 2026 |title=Trump Says He Has 'No Time Limits' on How Long War with Iran Could Go On |url=https://www.cnn.com/world/live-news/iran-war-us-israel-trump-03-05-26 |access-date=6 March 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=5 March 2026 |title=Hegseth Says the US Has "Only Just Begun to Fight" in War with Iran |url=https://www.cnn.com/world/live-news/iran-war-us-israel-trump-03-05-26 |access-date=6 March 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref> The Iranian tanker {{ship|IRIS|Bushehr}} was interned by the [[Sri Lanka Navy]], marking the first instance of a warship being interned in a neutral country since World War II.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=5 March 2026 |title=Sri Lanka Takes Control of Iranian Ship Iris Bushehr and 208 Crew |url=https://english.newsfirst.lk/2026/3/5/sri-lanka-takes-control-of-iranian-ship-iris-bushehr-and-208-crew |access-date=6 March 2026 |website=News First |language=en}}</ref>

=== Second week (7–13 March) ===
{{Further|2026 Qeshm Island desalination plant attack|2026 Iranian supreme leader election}}

On 7 March, the US sent a third aircraft carrier, {{USS|George H. W. Bush}}, to the Middle East.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=7 March 2026 |title=Operation Epic Fury: Is US Deploying 3Rd Carrier, USS George H.W. Bush (CVN-77), To The Middle East Amid Iran War? Here's All We Know |url=https://www.freepressjournal.in/world/operation-epic-fury-is-us-deploying-3rd-carrier-uss-george-hw-bush-cvn77-to-the-middle-east-amid-iran-war-heres-all-we-know |access-date=7 March 2026 |website=Free Press Journal |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Shelbourne |first=Mallory |date=6 March 2026 |title=USS Gerald R. Ford Now in the Red Sea, USS George H.W. Bush Wraps Pre-Deployment Exercises |url=https://news.usni.org/2026/03/06/uss-gerald-r-ford-now-in-the-red-sea-uss-george-h-w-bush-wraps-pre-deployment-exercises |access-date=7 March 2026 |website=USNI News |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=7 March 2026 |first=Ilgar |last=Khudiyev |title=US Said Expected to Deploy 3Rd Aircraft Carrier to the Middle East |url=https://en.apa.az/america/us-said-expected-to-deploy-3rd-aircraft-carrier-to-the-middle-east-495510 |access-date=7 March 2026 |website=[[Azerbaijani Press Agency]]}}</ref> The British aircraft carrier [[HMS Prince of Wales (R09)|HMS ''Prince of Wales'']] was placed on advanced readiness to defend British interests in the region.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=7 March 2026 |title=British Aircraft Carrier HMS Prince of Wales Prepped to Set Sail |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c39w2nj1rk8o |access-date=7 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> On 7 March, Iranian president [[Masoud Pezeshkian]] apologized for strikes on neighboring countries, citing "miscommunication in the ranks. He stated those countries would not be targeted unless the US launched attacks from them;<ref>{{Cite web|date=7 March 2026|title=Iran President Pezeshkian Apologises to Neighbours for Attacks, Tells Trump to Take 'Tehran Surrender Dream to Grave|url=https://indianexpress.com/article/world/iran-president-pezeshkian-apology-neighbours-trump-surrender-demand-10569646/|access-date=7 March 2026|website=The Indian Express|archive-date=8 March 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308213121/https://indianexpress.com/article/world/iran-president-pezeshkian-apology-neighbours-trump-surrender-demand-10569646/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="aljazeera7march"/> however, Iranian attacks continued, highlighting limited control over the IRGC chief [[Ahmad Vahidi]].<ref name="apnews20260307">{{Cite web|date=7 March 2026|title=Israel Renews Assault on Lebanon After Netanyahu Promises 'Many Surprises' in Next Phase of War|url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-israel-us-march-7-2026-d347fd6a03185f51d670bf4e7cbf5373|access-date=8 March 2026|website=[[Associated Press]]|quote=The message, seemingly filmed in a hurry, underlined the limited powers exercised by the theocracy's leaders over the paramilitary Revolutionary Guard. It answered only to Khamenei and now appears to be picking its own targets.|archive-date=12 March 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260312020811/https://apnews.com/article/iran-israel-us-march-7-2026-d347fd6a03185f51d670bf4e7cbf5373|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=8 March 2026|title=Strikes Continue Despite Iranian President's Apology|url=https://www.eurasiareview.com/08032026-strikes-continue-despite-iranian-presidents-apology/|work=Eurasia Review}}</ref><ref name="aljazeera7march">{{Cite web|date=7 March 2026|title=Iran to Halt Strikes on Neighbours Unless Attacks from There: Pezeshkian|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/7/iran-to-halt-strikes-on-neighbours-unless-attacks-from-there-pezeshkian|access-date=7 March 2026|website=Al Jazeera English|quote="The IRGC is now in charge fully, and they will decide whether to attack or not," Serdar said, adding that IRGC chief, Ahmad Vahidi, is considered one of the "most radical commanders" of the group since its foundation. "I don't think Pezeshkian or other politicians will have any influence when it comes to security politics," he added.|archive-date=10 March 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260310132001/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/7/iran-to-halt-strikes-on-neighbours-unless-attacks-from-there-pezeshkian|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 8 March, Khamenei's second son, [[Mojtaba Khamenei|Mojtaba]], was [[2026 Iranian supreme leader election|designated]] as Iran's new supreme leader.<ref name="AP timeline" /> [[US Central Command]] posted a message on [[X (social network)|X]] which urged "civilians in Iran to stay at home" and alleged that "[t]he Iranian regime is knowingly endangering innocent lives by using heavily populated civilian areas to conduct military operations, including launching one-way attack drones and ballistic missiles".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Ismay |first=John |date=8 March 2026 |title=U.S. Military Warns Civilians in Iran to Stay Home Amid Continuing Airstrikes |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/08/us/iran-us-warning-centcom-civilians.html |access-date=15 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>
[[File:P20260307DT-1619 The Dignified Transfer of Remains of Six U.S. Soldiers.jpg|thumb|Six dead US soldiers from the [[2026 Port Shuaiba drone attack]] are transferred to the US on 7 March 2026.|left]]
Israeli airstrikes hit Iranian oil storage facilities, killing four people.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=9 March 2026 |title=Iran Oil Facilities Hit for First Time as War with US-Israel Enters Day 9 |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/8/israel-strikes-irans-oil-facilities-for-first-time-as-war-enters-ninth-day |access-date=9 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> Strikes on fuel depots near Tehran caused a "river of fire" to pour out along the streets,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.timesnownews.com/world/middle-east/iran-war-oil-depot-strikes-videos-black-rain-us-israel-air-strikes-article-153787160 |title='River of Fire' in Tehran: Videos Show Israeli Strikes Hit Iran Fuel Depots, Trigger Black Rain |first=Rounak |last=Bagchi |date=9 March 2026 |website=Times Now}}</ref> and the city became engulfed in thick black smoke, causing toxic [[acid rain|acidic]] rain to fall in the surrounding area.<ref name="b673">{{cite magazine |last1=Schneid |first1=Rebecca |first2=Kay Armin |last2=Serjoie |last3=Jamalpour |first3=Fatemeh |title='The Air Is Unbreathable': Tehran Shrouded in Toxic Cloud After Israel Strikes Fuel Depots |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]] |date=8 March 2026 |url=https://time.com/7383099/iran-news-oil-strikes-tehran/ |access-date=10 March 2026 |quote=Both Israel and the U.S. military denied carrying out the [desalination plant] attack. |archive-date=28 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260328133020/https://time.com/7383099/iran-news-oil-strikes-tehran/ |url-status=dead}}</ref> Residents were advised by Iranian authorities to stay indoors, wear masks when outside, and conserve food and fuel.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Parent |first=Deepa |title='Dark, Like Our Future': Iranians Describe Scenes of Catastrophe After Tehran's Oil Depots Bombed |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=8 March 2026 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/08/dark-like-our-future-iranians-describe-scenes-of-catastrophe-after-tehrans-oil-depots-bombed |access-date=9 March 2026}}</ref> Kuwait reported that two of its officers were killed.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=8 March 2026 |title=Kuwait City Tower Erupts in Flames as Iran Launches New Wave of Strikes in the Gulf |url=https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/middle-east/kuwait-city-tower-fire-drones-iran-war-b2934196.html |access-date=8 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Din |first1=Menna |last2=Muhammad |first2=Al Gebaly |last3=Baum |first3=Bernadette |date=8 March 2026 |title=Two Kuwaiti Interior Ministry Officers Killed 'While Performing Duties' |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/two-kuwait-fire-officers-killed-while-performing-duties-fire-force-says-2026-03-08/ |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> The [[Saudi Civil Defense]] agency said that a strike on a compound in [[Al-Kharj]] killed two people.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=8 March 2026 |title=2 Killed, 12 Wounded After Projectile Hits Building in Saudi Arabia |url=https://aje.news/64yl8m?update=4378860 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref> US Central Command announced the death of a seventh US service member from an Iranian attack.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=8 March 2026 |title=US Troop Dies from Wounds Sustained in Iran Attack |url=https://aje.news/64yl8m?update=4379695 |access-date=8 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref>

The UK confirmed its forces had intercepted an Iranian drone headed towards Iraq, and declared its intention to send a [[Merlin helicopter]] to the region to detect aerial threats.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Kelliher |first1=Fiona |last2=Magee |first2=Caolán |date=8 March 2026 |title='Projectile' Kills 2 in Saudi Arabia as Iran Attacks on the Gulf Continue |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/8/iran-live-israel-bombs-tehran-oil-depots-attacks-on-gulf-states-continue |access-date=8 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> According to the [[Iranian Red Crescent Society]], 65 schools and 32 medical facilities had been targeted, and more than 10,000 civilian sites damaged.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=8 March 2026 |title=More on Civilian Sites Attacked in Iran: Red Crescent |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/8/iran-live-israel-bombs-tehran-oil-depots-attacks-on-gulf-states-continue?update=4379534 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |access-date=9 March 2026 |language=en}}</ref> On 9 March, NATO confirmed the interception of a second ballistic missile in Turkish airspace.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=9 March 2026 |title=NATO Intercepts Second Iranian Ballistic Missile Fired Toward Turkey |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/turkey-says-second-iranian-ballistic-missile-shot-down-by-nato-defences-in-airspace |access-date=9 March 2026 |work=[[The Straits Times]] |language=en |issn=0585-3923}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=9 March 2026 |title=NATO Intercepts Iranian Ballistic Missile in Turkish Airspace, Türkiye's Defense Ministry Says |url=https://www.kurdistan24.net/en/story/899194/slug |access-date=9 March 2026 |website=[[Kurdistan24]] |language=en}}</ref> Turkey deployed six F-16s and air defence systems to [[Northern Cyprus]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=9 March 2026 |title=MSB: 6 Türk F-16'sı KKTC'ye Konuşlandırıldı |trans-title=MoD: Six Turkish F-16s have been deployed to Northern Cyprus |url=https://www.trthaber.com/haber/gundem/msb-6-turk-f-16si-kktcye-konuslandirildi-937063.html |access-date=9 March 2026 |work=[[TRT Haber]] |language=tr}}</ref>

Trump claimed that "the war is very complete, pretty much", after speaking with Russian president Putin,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Mangan |first=Dan |date=9 March 2026 |title=Trump Says Iran 'War Is Very Complete', Talks to Putin: Reports |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/09/trump-iran-war-end.html |access-date=9 March 2026 |work=[[CNBC]] |language=en}}</ref> and said "we already won the war in many ways."<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Trew |first=Bel |date=9 March 2026 |title=Iran-US War Latest: Israel Launches Widespread New Strikes as Iranian Ballistic Missile Shot Down in Nato Airspace |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/middle-east/iran-us-war-israel-trump-mojtaba-khamenei-uk-latest-b2934455.html |access-date=9 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref> He claimed that the Strait of Hormuz was open and expressed interest in taking it over from Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Jiang |first=Weijia |date=9 March 2026 |title=Trump Says "The War Is Very Complete," And He's Considering Taking over Strait of Hormuz |work=CBS News |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-iran-cbs-news-the-war-is-very-complete-strait-hormuz/ |access-date=27 March 2026}}</ref> Trump went back on some comments during a press conference later that day, supporting Defense Secretary Hegseth in stating that the war was just the "beginning of building a new country" and it would end "soon".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/09/world/iran-war-israel-trump-oil#iran-war-oil-trump |first=Anushka |last=Patil |newspaper=[[The New York Times]] |title=Here's What Happened in the Conflict on Monday. |date=9 March 2026 |access-date=9 March 2026}}</ref> Following Syrian president Ahmed al-Sharaa's support for the Lebanon's objective to disarm Hezbollah,<ref name="Middle East Eye-2">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=9 March 2026 |title=Syrian President Backs Lebanon's Position on Disarming Hezbollah |url=https://www.middleeasteye.net/live-blog/live-blog-update/syrian-president-backs-lebanons-position-disarming-hezbollah |access-date=10 March 2026 |work=[[Middle East Eye]] |language=en}}</ref> the group [[2026 strikes on Syria during the Iran War|targeted]] the city of [[Inkhil]] in Syria.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=10 March 2026 |title=Israeli Army Intercepts Iranian Drone over Southern Syria: Report |url=https://aje.news/4oungf?update=4384727 |access-date=10 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref> About a dozen [[Rockwell B-1 Lancer|B-1B bombers]] arrived at bases in Europe.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=South |first=Todd |date=9 March 2026 |title=B-1s And B-52s Bombers Pour into Europe for Ops Against Iran |url=https://www.airandspaceforces.com/b-1s-b-52s-bombers-europe-iran-epic-fury/ |access-date=10 March 2026 |website=Air & Space Forces Magazine |language=en-US}}</ref>

[[File:Strait of Hormuz Transits.webp|thumb|{{center|Strait of Hormuz transits dropped significantly since the start of the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://portwatch.imf.org/pages/cc317ba850e34c4dadbead6f7b336fb1 |title=Trade Disruptions in the Strait of Hormuz Due to Attacks on Commercial Ships |website=PortWatch |publisher=[[International Monetary Fund]] |access-date=14 March 2026 |date=28 February 2026}}</ref>}}]]
[[GPS jamming]] of uncertain origin disrupted navigation of ships near the Strait of Hormuz.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c3ewwlx9e1xo |title=GPS Jamming: The Invisible Battle in the Middle East |last=Baraniuk |first=Chris |work=[[BBC News]] |date=10 March 2026 |language=en-GB}}</ref> The [[United States Department of State]]<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=11 March 2026 |title=Saudi Arabia Welcomes US Designation of Sudanese Muslim Brotherhood as Terrorist Organization |url=https://www.arabnews.com/node/2636030/amp |access-date=11 March 2026 |website=Arab News |language=en}}</ref> designated the [[Muslim Brotherhood]] branch in [[Sudan]] as a [[terrorist organization]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=9 March 2026 |title=U.S. Designates Sudanese Islamic Movement and Its Armed Wing as Terrorist Entity |url=https://sudantribune.com/article/311544 |access-date=11 March 2026 |website=Sudan Tribune |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Hendawi |first=Hamza |date=11 March 2026 |title=US Says Iran's IRGC-Trained Sudanese Muslim Brotherhood Members Fighting Alongside Army |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/03/11/us-says-irans-irgc-trained-sudanese-muslim-brotherhood-members-fighting-alongside-army/ |access-date=11 March 2026 |work=[[The National (Abu Dhabi)|The National]] |language=en}}</ref> On 10 March, an IRGC commander stated that Iran was only firing missiles with payloads of 1,000&nbsp;kg or more.<ref name="ndtv10march">{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-israel-war-iran-1000kg-1-ton-missile-warheads-iran-fires-khorramshahr-kheibar-shekan-missiles-11193972 |title=With Missiles Carrying 1,000 kg Explosives, A New Tactical Phase For Iran |work=[[NDTV]] |date=10 March 2026 |access-date=12 March 2026 |last=Srinivasan |first=Chandrashekar}}</ref> AFP reported that Iran's attacks were the "most intense and heaviest" since the start of the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Trew |first=Bel |date=10 March 2026 |title=Iran-US War Latest: Trump Threatens Heavy Escalation After Iran 'Begins Laying Mines in Strait of Hormuz' |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/middle-east/iran-us-trump-war-oil-prices-israel-qatar-latest-news-b2935224.html |access-date=11 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref> This showed a shift in tactics from saturating air defences to high-impact penetration strikes.<ref name="ndtv10march"/> American general [[Dan Caine]] acknowledged that Iran was fighting back, but not harder than the US expected.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 March 2026 |title=Iran Fighting Back but Not Stronger Than U.S. Thought, Top U.S. General Says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us-military-striking-iranian-mine-laying-vessels-top-us-general-says-2026-03-10/ |access-date=11 March 2026 |website=Reuters |language=en}}</ref>

Following the Syrian presidency's support for the disarmament of Hezbollah and a campaign of mobilization by the Syrian army on the Lebanese border,<ref name="Middle East Eye-2"/><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Chbaro |first=Asrar |date=6 March 2026 |title=What's Going on the Lebanon–Syria Border? |url=https://alhurra.com/en/15595 |access-date=10 March 2026 |website=Alhurra |language=en-US}}</ref> shells from Lebanon landed in [[Serghaya]], {{cvt|20|km}} from Damascus where the [[Syrian Armed Forces]] forces presided.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=10 March 2026 |title=Shells Fired From Lebanon Land West of Syrian Capital, Country's Military Says |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/world/middleeast/syria-hezbollah-iran-lebanon.html |url-access=registration |access-date=10 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> Israel issued an urgent evacuation notice to southern suburbs of Beirut.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=10 March 2026 |title=Urgent Israeli Warning for Residents of Southern Suburbs of Beirut: Evacuate Immediately |url=https://www.lbcgroup.tv/news/lebanon-news/912936/lbci-lebanon-articles/en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260420015503/https://www.lbcgroup.tv/news/lebanon-news/912936/lbci-lebanon-articles/en |archive-date=20 April 2026 |access-date=10 March 2026 |website=LBCIV7 |language=en}}</ref>

Defense analyst AJ Jaff reported that Iran's ballistic missile launch rate fell 92% from day one of the war (480 to 40) and the drone launch rate fell 92% (720 to 60).<ref name="jpost10march"/> On 11 March 14 US bombers were deployed to [[RAF Fairford]] in the UK, where bombs were being prepared for loading. This followed US war secretary Hegseth's statement that it was the "most intense day of strikes inside Iran".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Ambrose |first1=Tom |last2=Ho |first2=Vivian |last3=Corlett |first3=Eva |date=11 March 2026 |title=Middle East Crisis Live: Three Ships Hit in Strait of Hormuz as Iran Calls Vessels Belonging to US or Allies 'Legitimate Targets' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/11/iran-war-live-updates-trump-oil-hormuz-protestors-us-israel-beirut-middle-east-latest-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-69b1576c8f0828aedd6b1e1c#block-69b1576c8f0828aedd6b1e1c |access-date=11 March 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

Israel reportedly struck the [[Parchin]] military complex.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=12 March 2026 |title=Israel Says Strike Hit Iranian Nuclear-Linked Site Outside Tehran |url=https://themedialine.org/mideast-daily-news/israel-says-strike-hit-iranian-nuclear-linked-site-in-tehran/ |website=The Media Line |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=12 March 2026 |title=Post-Attack Assessment of Precision Strikes on the Bunkered Taleghan 2 Facility |url=https://isis-online.org/isis-reports/post-attack-assessment-of-precision-strikes-on-the-bunkered-taleghan-2-facility |website=Institute for Science and International Security |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=12 March 2026 |title=Iran Update Morning Special Report, March 12, 2026 |url=https://understandingwar.org/research/middle-east/iran-update-morning-special-report-march-12-2026/ |website=Institute for the Study of War |language=en}}</ref> A branch of [[Bank Sepah]] in Tehran was hit by a strike, prompting the IRGC to warn that they could retaliate by striking US or Israeli banks in the region.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=11 March 2026 |title=Missile Strike Hits Bank Sepah Branch in Tehran, IRGC Warns of Retaliation |url=https://iranwire.com/en/news/150256-missile-strike-hits-bank-sepah-branch-in-tehran-irgc-warns-of-retaliation/ |access-date=12 March 2026 |website=iranwire |language=en}}</ref> Iran hit [[Stryker Corporation|Stryker]], a US-based medical supply company with a cyberattack.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=12 March 2026 |title=Iran Appears to Have Conducted a Significant Cyberattack Against a U.S. Company, A First Since the War Started |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/iran-appears-conducted-significant-cyberattack-us-company-first-war-st-rcna263084 |access-date=12 March 2026 |work=[[NBC News]] |language=en}}</ref> On 12 March, [[UNICEF]] reported that 300 children had been killed, thousands injured, hundreds of thousands displaced, and millions unable to attend schools due to the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Rowlands |first1=Lyndal |last2=Sabah |first2=Zaid |date=12 March 2026 |title=Iran Sets Three Conditions for Peace; Oil Tankers in Iraqi Port Attacked |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/12/iran-war-live-oil-tankers-hit-in-iraq-tehran-sets-3-conditions-for-peace |access-date=12 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref>

Iranian deputy [[Ministry of Intelligence (Iran)|intelligence minister]] Akbar Ghaffari was killed in an airstrike.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=12 March 2026 |title=Iran Deputy Intelligence Minister Killed in Strikes on Tehran |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603125490 |access-date=12 March 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> An Iranian attack set two tankers on fire off the Iraqi coast, killing one person.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Yoon |first1=John |last2=Solomon |first2=Erika |date=12 March 2026 |title=Deadly Attack on Oil Tankers Prompts Iraq to Close Oil Terminals |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/12/world/middleeast/iraq-oil-tankers-attack-iran-war.html |access-date=12 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> The historical [[Safavid]]-era building of [[Rashk-e Jenan]], was destroyed by US-Israeli strikes.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=12 March 2026 |title=Day 13 of the U.S.-Israeli War on Iran: More Than Three Million Displaced |url=https://www.en-hrana.org/day-thirteen-of-the-u-s-israeli-war-on-iran-more-than-three-million-displaced/ |access-date=13 March 2026 |website=HRANA}}</ref> Other buildings damaged included the [[Chehel Sotoun]] pavilion, [[Rakib Khaneh Mansion]], [[Timurid Hall]], [[Ashraf Hall]] and the [[Ali Qapu]] palace.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=12 March 2026 |title=آسیب به چند بنای تاریخی در حمله اسرائیل به اصفهان |url=https://iranwire.com/fa/news-1/150147-%D8%A2%D8%B3%DB%8C%D8%A8-%D8%A8%D9%87-%DA%86%D9%86%D8%AF-%D8%A8%D9%86%D8%A7%DB%8C-%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AE%DB%8C-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D8%AD%D9%85%D9%84%D9%87-%D8%A7%D8%B3%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%A6%DB%8C%D9%84-%D8%A8%D9%87-%D8%A7%D8%B5%D9%81%D9%87%D8%A7%D9%86/ |access-date=13 March 2026 |website=iranwire |language=fa}}</ref> Many affected buildings and monuments were legally protected by the [[Blue Shield International]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Sinaiee |first=Maryam |date=13 March 2026 |title=War Leaves Its Mark on Iran's Cultural Heritage |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603125055 |access-date=13 March 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> which called damaging them a war crime.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=10 March 2026 |title=Blue Shield Warns of Potential 'War Crimes' Against Iran's Cultural Sites |url=https://www.museumsassociation.org/museums-journal/news/2026/03/blue-shield-warns-of-potential-war-crimes-against-irans-cultural-sites/ |access-date=13 March 2026 |website=Museums Association |language=en-US}}</ref> French soldiers were injured in a drone strike at a base in Iraqi Kurdistan. French president [[Emmanuel Macron]] announced on 13&nbsp;March that a soldier was killed in the attack.<ref name="lm13march">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=13 March 2026 |title=French Soldier Killed and Several Wounded in Attack in Iraq's Kurdistan Region, Confirms Macron |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/13/french-soldier-killed-in-attack-in-iraq-s-kurdistan-region-confirms-macron_6751397_4.html |access-date=13 March 2026 |work=[[Le Monde]]}}</ref>

[[File:Salalah Port Ablaze.jpg|thumb|Satellite imagery of black smoke rising from the [[Port of Salalah]] on 13 March during the [[2026 Iranian strikes on Oman]]]]
On 13 March, to help deal with the economic costs of the war, the US temporarily lifted restrictions on the sale of Russian oil.<ref name="Cooper">{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Cooper |first1=Helene |last2=Barnes |first2=Julian E. |last3=Ward |first3=Euan |last4=Torbati |first4=Yeganeh |last5=Reiss |first5=Johnatan |date=12 March 2026 |title=Iran War Live Updates: U.S. Refueling Plane Crashes in Iraq, Military Says |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/12/world/iran-war-news-trump-oil-israel |access-date=13 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Iran announced a coordinated offensive by its navy, army, and Hezbollah against Israel and US bases.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/live/cly0lwzk2ryt |script-title=fa:سنتکام: بمب‌افکن‌های بی‌۲ برای انجام عملیات در ایران به پرواز درآمدند |title= |trans-title= |date=14 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News Persian]] |language=fa}}</ref> Israel reported that 58 people have been hospitalized due to injuries following a missile strike.<ref name="Cooper" /> Kuwait authorities stated that defense equipment and the country's main airport were attacked, and power lines gone out of service.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=13 March 2026 |title=Iran Targets Gulf Nations with Missiles, Drones as Oil Prices Soar |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/12/iran-targets-gulf-nations-with-missiles-drones-as-oil-prices-soar |access-date=12 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> Missiles entered Turkish air space and were intercepted, with explosions heard near [[Adana]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=13 March 2026 |title=Nato Shoots Down Iranian Missile as Explosions Heard at Turkish Air Base |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news/nato-incirlik-air-base-missile-iran-war-b2937948.html |access-date=13 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref> Israel struck IRGC checkpoints after receiving tip-offs by on the ground informants. Reuters reported Israel had struck positions of the Basij used to suppress Iranian protests.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=13 March 2026 |title=Israel Targets Iranian Checkpoints Using Tip-Offs From Informants, Source Says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-targets-iranian-checkpoints-using-tip-offs-informants-source-says-2026-03-13/ |work=Reuters}}</ref>

=== Third week (14–20 March) ===
{{further|2026 Kharg Island attack|Assassination of Ali Larijani|2026 South Pars field attack}}

[[File:جزیره خارک- طبیعت و صنعت-10.jpg|thumb|[[Kharg Island]] in 2015; the fires on the towers are a normal part of oil refining.]]
As of the third week, analysts found little evidence of significant defections in the Iranian military,{{Efn|Multiple sources: <ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Graham-Harrison |first1=Emma |title=We Attacked Iran with No Clear Plan for Regime Change, Israeli Security Sources Say |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/12/israel-iran-us-attack-no-plan-for-regime-change-security-sources |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=12 March 2026 |quote=There have been no signs of Iranians taking to the streets or significant defections from security forces}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title='Odsečete Jednu Glavu, Izraste Nova': Kako Su Vladari Irana Stvorili Sistem Koji Ih Održava Na Vlasti |trans-title='You cut off one head, another grows': How Iran's rulers created a system that keeps them in power |url=https://www.bbc.com/serbian/articles/c99j8nzr01vo/lat |work=BBC Serbian |language=sh |date=12 March 2026 |quote=we hardly see any defections}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Iran War Becomes Contest of Who Can Take Most Pain |url=https://dailypioneer.com/news/iran-war-becomes-contest-of-who-can-take-most-pain |work=The Pioneer |date=12 March 2026 |quote=So far, the Islamic Republic has been able to keep its leadership and military cohesive and in control}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Is the Stability of the Iranian Regime in Danger? |url=https://www.inss.org.il/social_media/is-the-stability-of-the-iranian-regime-in-danger/ |website=Institute for National Security Studies |date=12 March 2026 |quote=However, it seems that at this stage, these strikes are not sufficient to undermine the internal cohesion among the security forces, their ability to function}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=US Intelligence Says Iran Government Is Not at Risk of Collapse, Say Sources |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/us-intelligence-says-iran-government-is-not-risk-collapse-say-sources-2026-03-11/ |work=Reuters |date=11 March 2026 |quote=The intelligence reporting underscores the cohesion of Iran's clerical leadership}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last1=Karlin |first1=Mara |title=Can Iran's Regime Survive the War? |url=https://www.brookings.edu/articles/can-irans-regime-survive-the-war/ |website=Brookings Institution |date=11 March 2026 |quote=is anyone defecting? Is anyone pulling away from the military, pulling away from the security services, and either taking their weapons and staying home or taking their weapons and acting against the regime? I haven't seen much on that front whatsoever.}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=The Six Pillars Keeping Iran's Regime Standing |url=https://www.thebeiruter.com/article/the-six-pillars-keeping-iran%E2%80%99s-regime-standing/1273 |website=The Beiruter |date=11 March 2026 |quote=Second, elite cohesion remains relatively strong.}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=A Long Road to the End: The Death Throes of Iran's Regime Could Last for Years |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/a-long-road-to-the-end-the-death-throes-of-irans-regime-could-last-for-years/ |work=The Times of Israel |date=10 March 2026 |quote=for now, there have been no significant defections from the army or other security forces}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=U.S. Intelligence Says Iran's Regime Is Consolidating Power |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/03/16/iran-regime-intelligence-irgc-war/ |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] |date=16 March 2026 |quote=Nonetheless, officials and analysts say, there are no overt signs of cracks or defections within Iran's power structure.}}</ref>}} which have been considered a necessary condition for [[regime change]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Jansen |first=Michael |title=Regime Change in Iran Unlikely Without Mass Defections from Military |url=https://www.irishtimes.com/world/middle-east/2026/02/28/regime-change-in-iran-unlikely-without-mass-defections-from-military/ |newspaper=[[The Irish Times]] |date=28 February 2026}}</ref> The US [[2026 Kharg Island attack|conducted an attack]] on [[Kharg Island]], a key oil export hub home to 90 percent of Iran's oil exports. Over 90 military sites were targeted while the oil infrastructure was not targeted "for reasons of decency", according to Trump.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Broadwater |first1=Luke |last2=Schmitt |first2=Eric |last3=Cooper |first3=Helene |last4=Pérez-Peña |first4=Richard |date=13 March 2026 |title=Iran War Live Updates: U.S. Military Attacks Kharg Island, Iran's Oil Export Hub, Trump Says |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/13/world/iran-war-trump-oil-israel |access-date=14 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-strikes-more-than-90-iranian-military-targets-kharg-island-centcom-says-2026-03-14/ |title=US Strikes More Than 90 Iranian Military Targets on Kharg Island, CENTCOM Says |agency=[[Reuters]] |date=14 March 2026}}</ref> On 14{{nbsp}}March, [[Kata'ib Hezbollah]] security commander Abu Ali al-Askari was killed in an airstrike in Baghdad.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Security Commander of Iraq's Kataeb Hezbollah Said Killed in Airstrike |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/security-commander-of-iraqs-kataeb-hezbollah-said-killed-in-airstrike/ |access-date=17 March 2026 |date=16 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]]}}</ref>

The [[Royal Tulip Al Rasheed Hotel]] in Baghdad's [[Green Zone]] was hit by a drone whilst hosting an EU and Saudi Arabian delegation. The attack was not claimed by anyone; however, due to the proximity of a similar attack 48{{nbsp}}hours earlier on the US embassy in Baghdad, there were suspicions it was an Iranian attack.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Abdelwahed |first=Mahmoud |date=16 March 2026 |title=Unclear Who Attacked Posh Baghdad Hotel in Iraq's 'Green Zone' |url=https://aje.news/s2q1rc?update=4405951 |access-date=16 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref>

[[File:Missile interception fragments of an Iranian missile hit Haifa oil refineries in Haifa Bay, March, 19 2026.jpg|thumb|upright=.8|An Iranian missile hit Haifa oil refineries in [[Haifa Bay]], 19 March]]
On 16 March, China and US-aligned [[NATO]] nations in Europe rejected Trump's call to provide military support to reopen the Strait of Hormuz.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/us-allies-respond-trump-strait-of-hormuz-demands-nato-iran-war-rcna263650 |title='Not Our War': U.S. Allies Balk at Trump's Strait of Hormuz Demands |first=Alexander |last=Smith |work=[[NBC News]] |date=16 March 2026 |access-date=17 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=16 March 2026 |title=Trump Demands NATO and China Police the Strait of Hormuz. So Far They Aren't Joining |work=NPR |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/03/16/nx-s1-5749109/trump-threatens-nato-strait-hormuz-iran-war |access-date=30 March 2026}}</ref> Trump rebuked his NATO allies, calling their decision a "very foolish mistake".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=17 March 2026 |title=Trump Says NATO's Refusal to Help on Iran Is "Very Foolish Mistake" |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/nato-countries-dont-want-get-involved-iran-operation-trump-says-2026-03-17/ |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> On the same day, White House Press Secretary [[Karoline Leavitt]] stated that the [[Second presidency of Donald Trump|Trump administration]] will not rule out [[Conscription in the United States|a military draft]] for the war. While doing so, she clarified that a draft is not "part of the current plan," but that the president is open to any suggestions.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.newsnationnow.com/us-news/military/trump-military-draft-iran/|title=Is a Military Draft Under Consideration with Iran War?|work=[[NewsNation]]|date=16 March 2026}}</ref> On 17 March, Trump made a statement on [[Truth Social]] renouncing NATO's assistance, and unexpectedly, US allies in the Indo-Pacific, namely Japan, South Korea, and [[Australian involvement in the 2026 Iran war|Australia]], for refusing to join US-led attacks on Iran during the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=17 March 2026 |title=NATO Countries Don't Want to Get Involved in Iran Operation, Trump Says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/nato-countries-dont-want-get-involved-iran-operation-trump-says-2026-03-17/ |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=17 March 2026 |title=Donald J. Trump (@realDonaldTrump) |url=https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/116245182325726375 |access-date=17 March 2026 |website=Truth Social |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |author=Kim Eun-bin |date=18 March 2026 |script-title=ko:트럼프 "이제 나토 도움 필요 없어...일본·한국도 마찬가지" |title= |trans-title= |url=https://www.joongang.co.kr/article/25412573 |access-date=17 March 2026 |script-newspaper=ko:중앙일보 |newspaper=Joong Ang Ilbo |trans-newspaper= |language=ko}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=18 March 2026 |url=https://www.khan.co.kr/article/202603180727001#ENT |script-title=ko:트럼프 "나토 도움 필요 없다...일본·호주·한국도 마찬가지" |title= |trans-title= |newspaper=[[Kyunghyang Shinmun]]}}</ref> Trump declared that the United States "[does] not need the help of anyone" regarding the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=17 March 2026 |title=Trump: 'We Do Not Need the Help of Anyone' |url=https://news.sky.com/video/trump-we-do-not-need-the-help-of-anyone-13520909 |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=[[Sky News]] |language=en}}</ref>

In the morning of 17 March, senior Iranian officials, including [[Ali Larijani]] and Basij chief [[Gholamreza Soleimani]] were [[Assassination of Ali Larijani|targeted by Israeli airstrikes]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=17 March 2026 |title=Israel Says It Killed Basij Commander Soleimani in Tehran Strike |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603178018 |access-date=17 March 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=17 March 2026 |title=Israeli Media Say Military Targeted Top Security Chief Larijani |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603174597 |access-date=17 March 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> Both their deaths were later confirmed by Iranian state media.<ref name="sk"/> In response, Iran launched a missile barrage that killed two Israeli civilians in [[Ramat Gan]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=18 March 2026 |title=Elderly Couple Killed in Iranian Revenge Strike on Israel |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/03/18/iran-war-latest-news-ali-larijani-death-tel-aviv-strikes/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]}}</ref> The same day, Israel launched a ground invasion of [[southern Lebanon]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Peled |first1=Anat |last2=Abdel-Baqui |first2=Omar |title=Israel Invades Lebanon, Opening New Front Against Iran |url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-invades-lebanon-opening-new-front-against-iran-f5e29555 |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=[[Wall Street Journal]] |date=16 March 2026}}</ref>

On 18 March,<ref name=blowup/> Israel [[2026 South Pars field attack|struck]] the [[South Pars/North Dome Gas-Condensate field|South Pars natural gas field]] in the Persian Gulf and its neighboring refineries in Iran with US coordination.<ref name="oj">{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Orr |first1=Robert |last2=Kelly |first2=Maxine |last3=Wells |first3=Peter |last4=Provan |first4=Sarah |last5=Cash |first5=Kieran |date=18 March 2026 |title=Middle East War Live: Oil Jumps After Iran Says Energy Industry Attacked |url=https://www.ft.com/content/6112e127-3ee2-4fce-acfc-f7644e5c6c30?syn-25a6b1a6=1 |work=[[Financial Times]]}}</ref> In retaliation, Iran attacked the world's largest LNG production facility in Qatar. Trump claimed he was unaware of the South Pars attack, promised that there would be no more Israeli attacks on Iranian oil infrastructure, and threatened Iran not to continue attacking Qatari energy infrastructure.<ref name=blowup>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Jones |first=Callum |date=19 March 2026 |title=Trump Threatens to 'Blow Up' All of Iran's South Pars Gasfield If Tehran Strikes Qatar |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/19/iran-war-trump-south-pars-threat-if-tehran-strikes-qatar |access-date=19 March 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-trump-says-no-more-israeli-attacks-on-south-pars/live-76422645 |title=Iran War: Netanyahu Denies Israel 'Dragged' US into Conflict |date=19 March 2026 |work=[[Deutsche Welle]]}}</ref> Israel said it had killed Iranian intelligence minister [[Esmaeil Khatib]] in an overnight airstrike.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=18 March 2026 |title=Israel Says It Killed Iran's Intelligence Chief After a Deadly Strike Near Tel Aviv |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/03/18/nx-s1-5751694/iran-retaliates-israel-kills-two-top-iranian-officials |access-date=18 March 2026 |work=[[NPR]] |language=en}}</ref> Pezeshkian confirmed Khatib's killing.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=18 March 2026 |title=Iran President Confirms Intelligence Minister Khatib Killed in Strike |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603187564 |access-date=18 March 2026 |work=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> A hair salon in [[Beit Awwa]] was [[2026 Beit Awwa salon strike|struck by a projectile]], killing four women,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Death Toll in Iranian Missile Strike That Hit West Bank Palestinian Town Rises to Four |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/death-toll-in-iranian-missile-strike-that-hit-west-bank-palestinian-town-rises-to-four/ |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |access-date=18 March 2026 |date=18 March 2026}}</ref> with Israeli authorities stating that it was most likely [[cluster munitions]] and Palestinian authorities saying it was an errant Israeli interceptor.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/19/world/iran-war-news-trump-oil |title=Iran War Live Updates: As Oil and Gas Prices Soar, Trump Seeks to Reassure Americans |first1=Tony |last1=Romm |first2=Isabel |last2=Kershner |first3=David E. |last3=Sanger |first4=Javier C. |last4=Hernández |first5=Johnatan |last5=Reiss |date=19 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=19 March 2026 |title=Three Palestinian Women Killed in Iranian Missile Attack in the West Bank, Red Crescent Says |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/three-palestinian-women-killed-in-iranian-missile-attack-in-the-west-bank-red-crescent-says?ref=latest |access-date=18 March 2026 |work=[[The Straits Times]] |language=en |issn=0585-3923}}</ref>

[[File:F-35 Lightning II fighter jet hit over Iran 2026.webm|thumb|thumbtime=00:06|Video of suspected Iranian strike on a USAF F-35, released by [[Tasnim News Agency]], 19 March 2026, the first case of a damaged stealth fighter in combat]]
On 19 March, a US [[F-35]] made an emergency landing after a suspected hit by Iranian forces.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Timotija |first=Filip |date=19 March 2026 |title=US F-35 Makes Emergency Landing After Flying over Iran |url=https://thehill.com/policy/defense/5792050-f35-emergency-landing-iran/ |access-date=19 March 2026 |work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=19 March 2026 |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/19/politics/f-35-damage-iran-war |title=US F-35 Damaged by Suspected Iranian Fire Makes Emergency Landing, Sources Say |work=[[CNN]]}}</ref> A [[BAZAN Group]] refinery in Haifa was hit during a broader Iranian missile attack on the area as a retaliation for Israeli attacks on South Pars gas facilities.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=20 March 2026 |title=Israeli Refinery Owner Says Essential Infrastructure Damaged in Iranian Strike |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/israeli-refinery-owner-says-essential-infrastructure-damaged-iranian-strike-2026-03-20/ |access-date=20 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=19 March 2026 |title=Damage at Haifa Oil Refineries After Iranian Missile Attack |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/h1rmbctqbl |access-date=19 March 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref> Netanyahu insisted that "You can't make a revolution from the air" and that "there must be a ground component—I won't share with you all the options", implying that there was a potential for limited assault operations involving soldiers on the ground in Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=19 March 2026 |title=Netanyahu: 'You Can't Make a Revolution from the Air, There Are Ground Options' |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/8148y4dvk |access-date=20 March 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref> The US began [[2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign|an aerial campaign]] against Iranian vessels and drones in the Strait of Hormuz in an effort to reopen it to international shipping.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Cloud |first1=David S. |last2=Seligman |first2=Lara |last3=Gordon |first3=Michael R. |date=20 March 2026 |title=U.S. War Planes and Helicopters Kick Off Battle to Reopen Hormuz |url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/u-s-war-planes-and-helicopters-kick-off-battle-to-reopen-hormuz-530cdb78 |access-date=20 March 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== Fourth week (21–27 March) ===
{{Further|2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign}}
Admiral [[Brad Cooper (admiral)|Brad Cooper]] said that the US military had so far struck more than 8,000 Iranian military targets, including 130 vessels.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Update from Eric Schmitt |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/21/world/iran-war-oil-trump/c56f7c98-40de-52bd-9442-0c5d3d640473?smid=url-share |access-date=21 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> On 21 March, the US conducted strikes on the [[Natanz Nuclear Facility]] using [[bunker buster]] bombs to target the site.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=US Strikes Iran's Natanz Nuclear Site with Bunker-Buster Bombs |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/03/21/us-strikes-irans-natanz-nuclear-site-bunker-buster-bombs/ |access-date=21 March 2026 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |language=en}}</ref> Russia condemned the strikes on Natanz as a "blatant violation of international law," while the IAEA urged military restraint "to avoid any risk of a nuclear accident".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Iran Says US and Israel Attacked Natanz Nuclear Facility |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/21/iran-says-us-and-israel-attacked-natanz-nuclear-facility |access-date=21 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> In response, Iran struck the southern Israeli town of [[Dimona]], injuring at least 78 people.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Iran War: Missiles Injure 160 in Towns Near Israeli Nuclear Site |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c9qdvnv13qdo |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> Iran said that it targeted the [[Shimon Peres Negev Nuclear Research Center]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Iranian Strike on Dimona Likely Targeted Israeli Nuclear Facility |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/ce84073mr06t?post=asset%3A2a437ed2-a431-4a86-a3e9-724c796dd1f2#post |access-date=21 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=21 March 2026 |title=Iran Targets Dimona Nuclear Facility as Response to Strike on Natanz |url=https://ilkha.com/english/world/iran-targets-dimona-nuclear-facility-as-response-to-strike-on-natanz-519569 |access-date=21 March 2026 |website=İlke Haber Ajansı |language=en}}</ref>

Citing unnamed US officials, CNN and ''The Wall Street Journal'' reported that Iran unsuccessfully attempted to strike the joint US–UK military base at [[Diego Garcia]] on the [[Chagos Archipelago|Chagos Islands]] in the [[British Indian Ocean Territory]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Foreign Secretary Denounces 'Reckless Iran Threats' After Missiles Fired at Diego Garcia |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yljdgwppzo |access-date=21 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> The report said one of the missiles broke apart mid-flight, while another was intercepted by a [[SM-3]] air defence missile launched by a US warship.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=20 March 2026 |title=Iran Targeted but Did Not Hit Diego Garcia Base with Missiles, WSJ Reports |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/iran-targeted-did-not-hit-diego-garcia-base-with-missiles-wsj-reports-2026-03-21/ |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> Israel said that Iran used a two-stage [[intercontinental ballistic missile]] to target the island.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Iran Launched Missiles at US-UK Military Base in the Indian Ocean. Here's What That Says About Its Capabilities |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/21/politics/iran-missiles-diego-garcia |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en |quote=Sam Lair, research associate at the James Martin Center for Nonproliferation Studies, told CNN that Iran's "space launch vehicles, including the (Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps') solid-propellant Ghaem-100, could clearly reach longer ranges than their regional missile force if they were used ballistically rather than as a space launch vehicle."}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=21 March 2026 |title=Iran's Missiles Are a Threat to London, Israel Warns After Attack on Diego Garcia |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/middle-east/iran-uk-missiles-distance-far-us-war-starmer-b2943167.html |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref> Iran denied launching missiles towards Diego Garcia, saying that it was an Israeli false flag attack.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=23 March 2026 |title='False Flag Attack': Iran Denies Claims It Fired Missiles at Diego Garcia |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/23/iran-denies-targeting-us-uk-diego-garcia-airbase-claims-false-flag-attack |access-date=23 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> In response the [[Foreign Secretary (United Kingdom)|UK Foreign Secretary]] confirmed and denounced the Iranian attack on their end, and additionally expanded permission for the United States to bomb certain targets using their bases.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Badshah |first1=Nadeem |last2=Ofori |first2=Morgan |date=21 March 2026 |title=UK Foreign Secretary Condemns Iran's 'Reckless Threats' After Strike Towards US-UK Base |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/21/iran-reportedly-fires-missiles-towards-uk-us-base-on-diego-garcia |access-date=14 May 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Mason |first1=Rowena |last2=Stewart |first2=Heather |last3=Topham |first3=Gwyn |last4=Elgot |first4=Jessica |date=21 March 2026 |title=Anger Grows Among UK Ministers Amid Fears Iran War Could Jeopardise Britain's Fragile Finances |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/20/uk-ministers-begin-contingency-planning-amid-fears-for-economic-effects-of-iran-war |access-date=14 May 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref> No evidence has been presented that the alleged Iranian missiles neared Diego Garcia or that one was intercepted.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last1=Vine |first1=David |title=Did Iran Attack Diego Garcia? |url=https://fpif.org/did-iran-attack-diego-garcia/ |website=fpif.org |publisher=Foreign Policy in Focus |access-date=27 March 2026 |date=25 March 2026}}</ref>

[[File:Operation-Roaring-Lion-0065.jpg|thumb|Israeli troops near the Lebanese border on 21 March 2026]]
The [[Houthis|Houthi movement]] in [[Yemen]] warned that it would respond to any escalation against Iran, including [[2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign|efforts to reopen the Strait of Hormuz]]. It specifically warned the two Arab countries offering to join the Strait of Hormuz campaign—Bahrain and the United Arab Emirates—that they "will be the first to lose in this battle".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Magdy |first=Samy |date=21 March 2026 |title=Houthi Rebels Say They Will Respond to Any Escalation Against Iran |url=https://apnews.com/live/iran-war-israel-trump-03-21-2026#0000019d-1258-dbe1-abff-3bfb86300000 |access-date=21 March 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref> The Houthis further threatened to join the war in the event that US allies joined the attack on Iran or if the US and Israel used the [[Red Sea]] to carry out operations.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=27 March 2026 |title=Update from James C. McKinley Jr. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/27/world/iran-war-trump-oil-israel/408e4a37-f012-504b-aeb9-05ccf81bf1af?smid=url-share |access-date=27 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Lebanon's government expelled the Iranian ambassador.<ref name="sl">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=26 March 2026 |title=How Long Will Israel Stay in Lebanon? |url=https://www.economist.com/middle-east-and-africa/2026/03/26/how-long-will-israel-stay-in-lebanon |access-date=26 March 2026 |newspaper=[[The Economist]] |issn=0013-0613}}</ref>

Trump issued an ultimatum to Iran, threatening to strike its [[power plants]] unless it opened the Strait of Hormuz within 48 hours.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=22 March 2026 |title=Update from David E. Sanger |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/21/world/iran-war-oil-trump/955f002b-7ace-562f-9659-32fe65eb3fe1 |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Iran doubled down, threatening to "completely" close the Strait of Hormuz and strike vital infrastructure across the region such as energy and [[desalination]] facilities critical for drinking water.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=22 March 2026 |title=Iran Threatens to 'Completely' Close Strait of Hormuz and Hit Power Plants After Trump's Ultimatum |url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-israel-trump-lebanon-march-22-2026-16cc60862529b873666ce4c1f6529d78 |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Iranian opposition]] figure and former crown prince [[Reza Pahlavi]] called on Trump and Netanyahu to target the military while sparing civilian infrastructure which "Iranians will need to rebuild our country."<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=22 March 2026 |title=Exiled Prince Pahlavi Urges US, Israel to Spare Iran Civilian Infrastructure |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603225840 |access-date=22 March 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> Halfway through the deadline, Trump announced that he was postponing strikes against Iranian power plants for five days,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=23 March 2026 |title=Trump Says He's Postponing Power Plant Strikes After US-Iran Talks - But Tehran Denies Talks Took Place |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/ce35wke27ynt?post=asset%3A6d3a3ec5-ef2a-47b9-b5b0-df4a2a9bffd8#post |access-date=23 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> and said the US was negotiating with Iran to end the war.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=23 March 2026 |title=Iran War: Trump Claims US Has Held Talks with Iran |url=https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-trump-claims-us-has-held-talks-with-iran/live-76478747 |access-date=23 March 2026 |website=[[Deutsche Welle]] |language=en}}</ref> Iran denied the talks ever took place or were taking place and called the president "deceitful".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=23 March 2026 |title=No Talks Are Underway Between Tehran and Washington, Iran Says |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603237530 |access-date=23 March 2026 |website=[[Iran International]] |language=en}}</ref> Iran rejected the 15-point peace plan presented by the US.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Sanger |first=David E. |date=25 March 2026 |title=U.S. Circulates Iran Peace Plan While Sending Troops to the Middle East |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/25/us/politics/iran-peace-plan-talks-trump.html |access-date=26 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |magazine |last=Sharp |first=Alexandra |date=26 March 2026 |title=Iran Rejects Trump's 15-Point Peace Plan |url=https://foreignpolicy.com/2026/03/25/iran-rejects-trump-15-point-peace-plan-us-war-strait-hormuz/ |access-date=26 March 2026 |magazine=[[Foreign Policy]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Iran asserted that Lebanon must be included as part of a ceasefire deal, thereby making a ceasefire conditional on an end to the [[2026 Lebanon war]] against Hezbollah.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Nakhoul |first1=Samia |last2=Bassam |first2=Laila |last3=Gebeily |first3=Maya |date=25 March 2026 |title=Iran Wants Lebanon Included in Any Ceasefire, Sources Say |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/iran-wants-lebanon-included-any-ceasefire-sources-say-2026-03-25/ |access-date=26 March 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref>

On 24 March, Israel or its allies shot down an Iranian missile crossing above Lebanon at high altitude, according to the Lebanese army, which also confirmed that the missile was not targeting Lebanon. This was the first time during the current conflict when a shootdown of an Iranian missile took place over Lebanese territory.<ref>{{#invoke:cite tweet| |number=2036480692641534409 |user=araReuters |title=2036480692641534409}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Berman |first1=Lazar |title=Lebanon Says It Was Not the Target of Iranian Missile That Blew up over Its Territory |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/lebanon-says-it-was-not-the-target-of-iranian-missile-that-blew-up-over-its-territory/ |access-date=29 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |date=25 March 2026}}</ref>

A US strike on the Habbaniya military base—which hosts units from the [[Popular Mobilization Forces]]—in [[Al Anbar Governorate]] killed seven members of the [[Iraqi Armed Forces]] and injured 13 others. In response, Iraqi prime minister [[Mohammed Shia' al-Sudani]] summoned the US embassy's [[chargé d'affaires]] in Baghdad.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Naar |first=Ismaeel |date=25 March 2026 |title=Iraq Summons U.S. Diplomat After Attack on Military Base |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/25/world/middleeast/iraq-summons-us-diplomat-after-attack-on-military-base.html |access-date=26 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Iranian state media threatened that Iran could seize Bahraini and Emirati territory if the US "makes any mistakes", while signaling its readiness to open a new front in Yemen by closing the [[Bab-el-Mandeb|Bab al-Mandab]] Strait together with the [[Houthis]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Berman |first=Lazar |date=25 March 2026 |title=Iran State Media Threatens Seizure of UAE and Bahrain Coastlines |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/iran-state-media-threatens-seizure-of-uae-and-bahrain-coastlines/ |access-date=25 March 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Holcman |first=Tobias |date=25 March 2026 |title=Iran Warns Its Ready to Open New Front in Yemen, Close Bab al-Mandab Strait with Houthis - Report |url=https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-891193 |access-date=26 March 2026 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]]}}</ref> Israel said it killed Iran's top naval commander, [[Alireza Tangsiri]], purportedly as part of an effort to reopen the Strait of Hormuz, which Katz said Tangsiri was "directly responsible" for the closure of.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=26 March 2026 |title=Israel Says It Killed Iran's Top Naval Commander in Bid to Reopen Strait of Hormuz |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/03/26/us-israel-iran-navy-chief-killed-hormuz/ |access-date=26 March 2026 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Torbati |first=Yeganeh |date=26 March 2026 |title=Who Is Alireza Tangsiri, The Latest Iranian Commander Targeted by Israel? |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/26/world/middleeast/who-alireza-tangsiri-iran-commander-navy-irgc.html |access-date=26 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=26 March 2026 |title=Israel Says It Has Killed Iran's Navy Chief Overseeing Strait of Hormuz Blockade |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy81p99x07no |access-date=26 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref>

On 27 March, a day after Trump and Hegseth announced the "neutralization" of Iran's military, an Iranian missile and drone strike on [[Prince Sultan Air Base]] damaged several US refueling aircraft and injured at least 15 US soldiers. An [[Boeing E-3 Sentry|E-3 Sentry]] was also damaged by the strike.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 March 2026 |title=US AWACS Aircraft Hit in Iran Strike: Damage to E-3 Sentry Raises Alarm over Airpower Blind Spots |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/world/us-awacs-aircraft-hit-in-iran-strike-damage-to-e-3-sentry-raises-alarm-over-airpower-blind-spots-article-13873517.html |work=Moneycontrol |access-date=29 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 March 2026 |title=12 US Troops Wounded in Iranian Strike on Saudi Base |url=https://www.freemalaysiatoday.com/category/world/2026/03/28/12-us-troops-wounded-in-iranian-strike-on-saudi-base |access-date=28 March 2026 |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]] |website=Free Malaysia Today |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="apnews27march">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=27 March 2026 |title=Yemen's Houthis Claim Responsibility for Missile Attack on Israel, Their First Since War Started |url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-israel-trump-lebanon-march-27-2026-195444c54cbb7545d0a77f8ffbc0e4c0 |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |quote=More than two dozen U.S. troops have been wounded in Iranian attacks on a Saudi air base in the past week, according two people who have been briefed on the matter. Iran fired six ballistic missiles and 29 drones at Saudi Arabia's Prince Sultan air base in a Friday attack that injured at least 15 troops, including five seriously, according to the people who were not authorized to comment publicly and spoke on the condition of anonymity. The base had come under come attack twice earlier this week, including an incident that injured 14 U.S. troops, according to the people who had been briefed on the matter. Located about 96 kilometers (60 miles) from the Saudi capital of Riyadh, the base is run by the Royal Saudi Air Force, but also used by U.S. troops.}}</ref> Military analyst Cedric Leighton described the attack as a "a serious blow to [US] surveillance capabilities".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/30/middleeast/us-air-force-awacs-jet-destroyed-saudi-arabia-intl-hnk-ml |title=Destruction of Vital US Radar Aircraft Could Hamper Ability to Spot Iran Threats, Analysts Say |first1=Brad |last1=Lendon |first2=Isaac |last2=Yee |first3=Thomas |last3=Bordeaux |date=30 March 2026 |work=[[CNN]]}}</ref> The same day, Iran blocked two Chinese ships from entering the strait and sought to formalize fees for ships passing through it.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-war-middle-east-news-updates?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=AWEtsqc-wFOitB0vwalUEiudO_jg00E9TkV34Imv8jJLGM3MxrRrvB-2I6b60J_TkzE%3D&gaa_ts=69c6b925&gaa_sig=8KvpNsolzIz3jNFVtMmGVyyMJMiLIuTHS-LsPLyFW5LSuKhmrgK5wNOH0yQ_ANyxsNheGp08TG8CdkyGnyrXBA%3D%3D |title=Iran Blocks Two Chinese Ships From Hormuz in Rare Move |newspaper=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |date=27 March 2026 |access-date=27 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Ward |first=Euan |date=27 March 2026 |title=Iran Moves to Formalize Toll Plan in Strait of Hormuz |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/27/world/middleeast/iran-hormuz-strait-tolls.html |access-date=27 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Despite pushes for talks, Israeli defense minister Israel Katz publicly vowed to "intensify and expand" Israeli attacks in Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/live-blog/live-updates-iran-war-trump-hormuz-markets-israel-tehran-rcna265440 |title=Live Updates: Israel Vows to 'Intensify and Expand' Iran Attacks; Trump Delays Strait of Hormuz Deadline |work=[[NBC News]] |date=27 March 2026 |access-date=27 March 2026}}</ref> The same day, the [[IR-40|Shahid Khondab Heavy Water Complex]] in Arak—which has in the past been used to test uranium enrichment—and the [[Nuclear facilities in Iran#Ardakan|Ardakan yellowcake production plant]] in Yazd Province were confirmed to have been damaged in Israeli airstrikes.<ref name=struckmarch2026>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-israel-trump-lebanon-march-27-2026-195444c54cbb7545d0a77f8ffbc0e4c0 |title=Iran Says It Will 'Facilitate and Expedite' Humanitarian Aid Through the Strait of Hormuz |first1=Jon |last1=Gambrell |first2=Farnoush |last2=Amiri |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=27 March 2026 |access-date=27 March 2026}}</ref><ref name=march2026struckairstrike>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-israel-hits-iranian-heavy-water-nuclear-reactor/live-76555531 |title=Iran War: Israel Hits Iranian Heavy Water Nuclear Reactor |work=[[Deutsche Welle]] |date=27 March 2026 |access-date=27 March 2026}}</ref>

=== Fifth week (28 March – 3 April) ===
{{Further|2026 Houthi strikes on Israel|Karaj B1 bridge attack}}
The Houthis joined the war on 28 March [[2026 Houthi strikes on Israel|launching a ballistic missile]] towards Israel.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Yemen's Houthis Claim First Missile Attack on Israel Since War Began |url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/yemens-houthis-claim-first-missile-attack-on-israel-since-war-began |access-date=5 April 2026 |work=[[PBS News Hour]] |agency=[[Associated Press]] |date=28 March 2026}}</ref> The Houthis said that they had launched ballistic missiles targeting "sensitive" military sites in Israel, and vowed to continue the attacks "until the aggression on all resistance fronts stops". The missile was intercepted and no casualties were reported.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Dahir |first1=Abdi Latif |last2=Sampson |first2=Eve |date=28 March 2026 |title=Yemen's Houthis Fire at Israel and Vow Further Attacks |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/28/world/middleeast/yemen-houthis-attack-israel-war.html |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> The Houthis subsequently launched a second missile at [[Eilat]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 March 2026 |title=Houthis Fired Second Missile at Israel, Security Official Says |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-war-middle-east-news-updates/card/houthis-fired-second-missile-at-israel-security-official-says-IFmP7oOU3SAsZN4ygirW |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref> In response, the internationally recognized [[Presidential Leadership Council|Yemeni government]] condemned Iran's "frequent attempts to drag Yemen" into conflict "through its terrorist militias".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 March 2026 |title=Yemen's Internationally-Recognised Government Accuses Iran of Dragging Country into Conflict |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/cje4x38q8xqt?post=asset%3A9b9dc9c4-0c3e-45dd-916a-863e48f34f0d#post |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> On the same day, 2,500 US marines from the [[31st Marine Expeditionary Unit]] arrived in the Middle East, expected to be part of US efforts to open the Strait of Hormuz.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 March 2026 |title=Update from Helene Cooper |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/28/world/iran-war-trump-israel-oil/06cca092-ddd6-5d3a-a460-2e70367fefe2?smid=url-share |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

[[US Central Command]] (CENTCOM) stated that it had struck over 11,000 targets in Iran since the beginning of the war. On 28 March, joint US–Israeli airstrikes severely damaged several residential and civilian facilities, including the [[Iran University of Science and Technology]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Baskar |first1=Pranav |last2=Hakim |first2=Shirin |date=28 March 2026 |title=Airstrikes Batter a University and Residential Zones in Tehran. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/28/world/iran-war-trump-israel-oil |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> In response, Iran threatened to attack Israeli and American colleges across the Middle East.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=29 March 2026 |title=Update from Sanam Mahoozi |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/29/world/iran-war-trump-israel-oil/9b3c6f7c-33ca-5d8e-aab0-912c41dc5b1c?smid=url-share |access-date=29 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Airstrikes also struck a {{Convert|10000|m3|adj=on}} water reservoir in [[Haftkel]], in [[Khuzestan province]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 March 2026 |title=Update from Shirin Hakim |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/28/world/iran-war-trump-israel-oil/2d66958d-1459-5acf-837a-bbcf91045cad?smid=url-share |access-date=28 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

An Iranian missile struck a chemical plant in the [[Ne'ot Hovav]] industrial zone, injuring one person and causing fears of a hazardous leak.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Pietromarchi |first1=Virginia |last2=Magee |first2=Caolán |date=29 March 2026 |title=Israeli Chemical Factory Attacked by Iranian Missile |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/3/29/iran-war-live-houthis-attack-israel-anti-war-protesters-rally-in-tel-aviv?update=4444292 |access-date=29 March 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> A convoy of the Iraqi Popular Mobilization Forces was seen entering [[Khorramshahr]] in southwestern Iran.<ref name="iranintl28march">{{#invoke:cite |web |date=28 March 2026 |title=Video: Tehran-Backed Militia Convoy Seen Moving from Iraq Toward Iran |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603282000 |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=Iran International |language=en}}</ref> Eleven-year-old [[child soldier]] [[Alireza Jafari (child soldier)|Alireza Jafari]] was killed in an Israeli drone strike "while serving" at a checkpoint on a Tehran highway;<ref>Habibiazad, Ghoncheh. [https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c9wqgjn7x89o "Iran using children in security roles in war, reports and witnesses say"], ''[[BBC News Persian]]'', 31 March 2026. Accessed 5 July 2026. "The death of an 11-year-old Iranian boy reportedly in an air strike while manning a security checkpoint alongside his father in Tehran has thrown focus on a new initiative to recruit children into the security services. Alireza Jafari's mother Sadaf Monfared told the municipality-run newspaper Hamshahri that the pair had been helping Basij volunteer militia patrols and checkpoints to 'maintain the security of Tehran and its people' when they were killed on 11 March."</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=30 March 2026 |script-title=fa:جذب کودکان ۱۲ ساله در ساختارهای امنیتی ایران و گزارش‌ها از کشته شدن یک کودک در تهران |title= |trans-title= |url=https://parsi.euronews.com/2026/03/30/iranian-security-structures-recruits-12-year-old-child-killed-in-tehran-reports |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=[[Euronews]] |language=fa}}</ref> [[Amnesty International]] called the organized Iranian recruitment of children as young as Jafari a [[war crime]].<ref>[https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/04/iran-recruitment-of-child-soldiers-as-young-as-12-amounts-to-a-war-crime/ "Iran: Recruitment of child soldiers as young as 12 amounts to a war crime"], 2 April 2026. Accessed 5 July 2026. "Iranian authorities are trampling upon children's rights and committing a grave violation of international humanitarian law amounting to a war crime by recruiting and mobilizing children as young as 12 into a military campaign led by the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC), Amnesty International said today.... On 29 March, 11-year-old boy, Alireza Jafari, was killed, while accompanying his father, a member of the IRGC's Basij, at a checkpoint in Tehran, laying bare the devastating consequences of the presence of children at military objectives. Authorities have confirmed that the child was killed 'while serving' at a checkpoint following an Israeli drone attack."</ref>

On 29 March, Trump stated that he would prefer to "take the [[Oil reserves in Iran|oil in Iran]]". He proposed taking Iran's oil export center, [[Kharg Island]], claiming that the United States could capture the territory "very easily", and implying that the US could occupy it for some time.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=30 March 2026 |title=Donald Trump Says US Could 'Take the Oil in Iran' |url=https://www.ft.com/content/3bd9fb6c-2985-4d24-b86b-23b7884031f5?syn-25a6b1a6=1 |access-date=30 March 2026 |work=[[Financial Times]] |language=en}}</ref>

On 30 March, Trump said that if a deal were not reached soon and the Strait of Hormuz reopened, the US would strike all of Iran's power plants, oil wells, Kharg Island, and possibly all its desalinization plants,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Bohner |first1=Athina |last2=Berry |first2=Alex |last3=Oelofse |first3=Louise |agency=AP, AFP, dpa, Reuters, EFE |date=30 March 2026 |title=Trump Again Threatens to 'Obliterate' Iranian Power Plants, Oil Wells and Kharg Island |url=https://p.dw.com/p/5BNQw |work=[[Deutsche Welle]] |access-date=30 March 2026}}</ref> although the feasibility and strategic value of some of Trump's threats were contested.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Daniel |last=Bush |date=7 April 2026 |title=What the US Military Could Do If Iran Fails to Meet Trump's Ultimatum |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c98kn1zlxr1o |access-date=11 April 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> On the same day Turkey and NATO intercepted the fourth missile directed towards Turkish territory. Iran denied firing a missile at Turkey, claiming that it was a [[false flag]] attack.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Hacaoglu |first1=Selcan |last2=Kozok |first2=Firat |date=30 March 2026 |title=NATO Downs New Iranian Missile in Escalating Turkey Threat |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-03-30/nato-intercepts-fourth-iranian-missile-targeting-turkey |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=[[Bloomberg News]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=31 March 2026 |title=Reports of Iranian Missile Launch Toward Turkey Are Completely Baseless |url=https://wanaen.com/reports-of-iranian-missile-launch-toward-turkey-are-completely-baseless/ |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=WANA News Agency}}</ref> The US began flying [[Boeing B-52 Stratofortress|B-52 bombers]] over Iranian territory for the first time, indicating its confidence of [[air supremacy]] over Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Jaffe |first1=Greg |last2=Ismay |first2=John |last3=Cooper |first3=Helene |last4=Fuller |first4=Thomas |date=31 March 2026 |title=Confident of Air Supremacy, U.S. Sends B-52 Bombers Over Iran |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/31/world/middleeast/us-iran-b52-bombers.html |access-date=1 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> The US used bombers to target an ammunition depot and air base in [[Isfahan]], causing large explosions.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Varghese |first1=Sanjana |last2=Boxerman |first2=Aaron |date=31 March 2026 |title=Trump Shares Video of Bombing in Iranian City of Isfahan |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/31/world/middleeast/isfahan-iran-bombing-trump-video.html |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> U.S-allied Gulf states such as Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Kuwait, and Bahrain reportedly pushed Trump to continue the war until there are significant changes in Iran's leadership.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Madhani |first1=Aamer |last2=Magdy |first2=Samy |last3=Lee |first3=Matthew |last4=Mednick |first4=Sam |date=30 March 2026 |title=Gulf Allies Privately Make the Case to Trump to Keep Fighting Until Iran Is Decisively Defeated |url=https://apnews.com/article/trump-iran-saudi-arabia-mbs-gulf-war-uae-89f690b952fe28d3140c537b70fa5051 |access-date=1 April 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref> American journalist [[Shelly Kittleson]] was kidnapped in Baghdad by [[Kata'ib Hezbollah]]—the strongest faction within the PMF—who demanded that the Iraqi government release several detained members of the group.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Solomon |first=Erika |last2=Hassan |first2=Falih |date=1 April 2026 |title=Iraqi Kidnappers of Journalist Shelly Kittleson Offer to Negotiate |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/01/world/middleeast/shelly-kittleson-kidnapping-iraq.html |access-date=2 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

On 1 April, [[Mehr News Agency]], a semi-official Iranian government news outlet, reported that policy expert and former foreign minister [[Kamal Kharazi]] was seriously injured and his wife was killed in an airstrike which hit his home.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=1 April 2026 |title=Former Iran FM 'Seriously Injured', Wife Killed in Tehran Strike |url=https://english.alarabiya.net/News/middle-east/2026/04/01/former-iran-fm-seriously-injured-wife-killed-in-tehran-strike |access-date=1 April 2026 |website=[[Al Arabiya English]] |language=en}}</ref> Iranian officials described the attack as an attempt to derail diplomacy, noting that Kharazi was overseeing a possible meeting between Iranian officials and US vice president [[JD Vance]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 April 2026 |title=Update from Farnaz Fassihi and Shirin Hakim |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/01/world/iran-war-trump-oil-news/939c1047-1929-5d6f-9440-2f4dbb2f12f8?smid=url-share |access-date=1 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Airstrikes on the strategically important [[Hengam Island]] in the Strait of Hormuz caused seven injuries.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 April 2026 |title=Update from Shirin Hakim |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/01/world/iran-war-trump-oil-news/c29ebf0b-3e93-5883-b793-d3a6d6e4da03?smid=url-share |access-date=1 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Netanyahu asserted that the US–Israeli strikes have eliminated Iran's ability to produce nuclear weapons and ballistic missiles, thereby removing "two existential threats" to Israel.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Rasgon |first=Adam |date=1 April 2026 |title=Netanyahu Makes the Case That Wars on Iran Have Succeeded. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/01/world/iran-war-trump-oil-news/netanyahu-israel-iran-war?smid=url-share |access-date=1 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

Late in the day on 1 April, Trump made a speech addressing the nation, in which he said that the strikes have "dramatically curtailed" Iranian missile and drone systems, and added that the attacks on Iran will escalate over the next two to three weeks to "bring them back to the [[Stone Age]]s, where they belong".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Broadwater |first=Luke |last2=Pager |first2=Tyler |date=2 April 2026 |title=5 Takeaways From Trump's Speech on Iran |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/01/us/politics/trump-iran-war-address-takeaways.html |access-date=2 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

On 2 April, [[Karaj B1 bridge attack|two US strikes]] on the [[Karaj B1 bridge|B1 bridge]] between Tehran and [[Karaj]], which was described as the highest bridge in the Middle East, reportedly killed eight people and wounded 95 others, causing it to collapse.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=2 April 2026 |title=Trump Announces Destruction of Iran's Tallest Bridge |url=https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/trump-announces-destruction-irans-tallest-bridge |access-date=2 April 2026 |agency=Agence France Presse |website=Al-Monitor |language=en}}</ref> Experts assessed the attack as a possible [[war crime]]; it was celebrated by Trump.<ref name="france24-2april">{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Trump Gloats on Possible War Crimes in Iran, But Punishment Distant |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260402-trump-gloats-on-possible-war-crimes-in-iran-but-punishment-distant |work=France 24 |date=2 April 2026 |language=en}}</ref> At the time of the attack, many Iranian families had been gathered in the parks below the bridge to celebrate [[Sizdah Be-dar]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/articles/cgk03vyre3ko |script-title=fa:واکنش‌ها یه حمله هوایی به «بلندترین پل خاورمیانه» در کرج؛ از نگرانی از بازگشت به «عصر حجر» تا «بهترش را می‌سازیم» |date=3 April 2026 |website=[[BBC News Persian]] |language=fa}}</ref>

Iran revealed major damage to the century-old medical center [[Pasteur Institute of Iran]]. US defense secretary Hegseth boasted of "death and destruction from the sky all day long".<ref name="france24-2april"/> The IDF also announced that one of its strikes in the [[Kermanshah]] area of Iran killed Iranian ballistics missile chief Makram Atimi and several battalion commanders from Atimi's central Iranian ballistic missile unit.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/article-891953 |title=IDF Kills Iranian Ballistic Missile Chief, US Strike Targets Key Supply Bridge in Tehran |first1=Tobias |last1=Siegel |first2=Sam |last2=Halperin |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |date=2 April 2026 |access-date=3 April 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.israelnationalnews.com/flashes/682113 |title=IDF Eliminates Iranian Ballistic Missile Commander in Kermanshah Region |work=[[Israel National News]] |date=2 April 2026 |access-date=3 April 2026}}</ref> An Iranian ballistic missile strike damaged an Israeli drone factory in [[Petah Tikva]].<ref name="calcalistech3april">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 April 2026 |title=Israeli Drone Factory Hit by Iranian Missile |url=https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/b1bptztoze |access-date=3 April 2026 |work=CTech}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 April 2026 |title=Iranian Missile Significantly Damages Aerosol Drone Company Factory in Petah Tikva |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/odko2iotd |access-date=3 April 2026 |work=[[Ynet]]}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=3 April 2026 |title=AeroSentinel Production Facility Severely Damaged After Iranian Ballistic Missile Strike |url=https://www.jpost.com/defense-and-tech/article-892002 |access-date=3 April 2026 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]]}}</ref> On the same day, [[Islamic Republic of Iran Army|Iran's army]] chief, [[Amir Hatami]], stated that if US forces invade the country, "not a single person" among the invaders will survive.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 April 2026 |title=Iran Army Chief Warns Against US Invasion |url=https://www.ptinews.com/detail/international/Iran-army-chief-warns-against-US-invasion/3523168 |access-date=3 July 2026 |agency=Associated Press|work=Press Trust of India}}</ref>

[[File:F15 Eagle - RAF Lakenheath (37835332816).jpg|thumb|An F-15E Strike Eagle of the 494th Fighter Squadron, similar to the American aircraft [[2026 United States F-15E rescue operation in Iran|shot down]]]]
On 3 April, Iranian forces shot down a US Air Force [[McDonnell Douglas F-15E Strike Eagle|F-15E Strike Eagle]] fighter jet over the country, with the wreckage falling in the [[Kohgiluyeh and Boyer-Ahmad province]] of Iran,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.dawn.com/news/1988377 |title=Another US Jet Shot Down as Iran War Escalates |date=4 April 2026 |website=Dawn}}</ref> the first incident of its kind in more than 20 years.<ref name="bbc7april">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2vpz1kwreo|title=How rescue of US airman in remote part of Iran unfolded|website=[[BBC News]]|date=7 April 2026}}</ref> The pilot was rescued that same day, but the [[Weapon systems officer|WSO]] remained missing and was [[2026 United States F-15E rescue operation in Iran|rescued alive 48 hours later]]<ref name="ap-f515e-rescue" /> in a "high-stake" operation involving US special forces supported by 155 aircraft.<ref name="bbc7april"/>

A US [[Fairchild Republic A-10 Thunderbolt II|A-10 "Warthog"]] aircraft was downed and its single crew member ejected near the Strait of Hormuz and was rescued.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Schmitt |first=Eric |last2=Cooper |first2=Helene |last3=Torbati |first3=Yeganeh |last4=Rasgon |first4=Adam |last5=Bergman |first5=Ronen |date=3 April 2026 |title=Iran War Live Updates: Downed U.S. Jet and Missing Crew Member Raise Stakes in War |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/03/world/iran-war-trump-oil |access-date=3 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Iran released a video showing shooting down the aircraft using surface-to-air missile.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |magazine |last1=Schneid |first1=Rebecca |title=Trump Claimed Total Control of Iran's Airspace. Then Two Warplanes Were Downed |url=https://time.com/article/2026/04/04/f-15-shot-down-iran-search/ |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]] |date=4 April 2026}}</ref>

On the same day, Tehran's [[Shahid Beheshti University]] was hit by airstrikes, making the total number of universities hit to more than 30, according to the Iranian Minister of Science.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Iranian Minister of Science: U.S.-Israeli Strikes Targeted 30 Universities Since Start of War |url=https://hawarnews.com/en/iranian-minister-of-science-us-israeli-strikes-targeted-30-universities-since-start-of-war |work=[[Hawar News]] |date=4 April 2026 |access-date=4 April 2026}}</ref>

===Sixth week (4–7 April)===
{{Further|2026 United States F-15E rescue operation in Iran|Destruction of the Rafi'-Nia synagogue}}

[[File:2026-04-07 Trump – A whole civilization will die tonight 2026-04-07 192815 (cropped).png|thumb|7 April: [[Truth Social]] post in which Trump threatened, "A whole civilization will die tonight, never to be brought back again."]]
On 4 April, explosions were reported at an auxiliary building of the [[Bushehr Nuclear Power Plant]] as well as the Mahshahr Special Petrochemical Zone in [[Bandar-e Mahshahr|Mahshahr]], Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/04/world/iran-war-trump-news |title=U.S. Rescues Downed Air Force Officer Deep Inside Iran, Trump Says |first1=Greg |last1=Jaffe |first2=Eric |last2=Schmitt |first3=Helene |last3=Cooper |date=4 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> The airstrikes in Mahshahr killed at least five and injured 170 others.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 April 2026 |title=Update from Shirin Hakim |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/04/world/iran-war-trump-news/f8c31573-78bc-5053-a5a0-99ce0bf46017?smid=url-share |access-date=4 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> An Iranian missile strike hit in the vicinity of the IDF's [[HaKirya]] headquarters in Tel Aviv.<ref name="jpost4april">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=4 April 2026 |title=WATCH: IDF Confirms Iranian Missile Fragments Hit Near Kirya, Multiple Cars Ablaze in Ramat Gan |url=https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/defense-news/article-892034 |access-date=4 April 2026 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en}}</ref>

On 5 April, after heavy fighting, the second stranded crew member from the F-15E downed on 3 April was recovered by US forces in a [[2026 United States pilot rescue operation in Iran|rescue operation]], which resulted in damage to helicopters, the shooting down of an [[A-10 Thunderbolt|A-10 Thunderbolt II]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last1=Stewart |first1=Phil |last2=Ali |first2=Idrees |title=High-Stakes US Special Forces Mission Rescues Airman from Iran After F-15 Crash |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-rescues-airman-whose-f-15-was-downed-iran-us-officials-say-2026-04-05/ |access-date=5 April 2026 |work=[[Reuters]] |date=5 April 2026}}</ref> and the destruction of two [[C-130|C-130 Hercules]], three IRGC members killed, and several American service members injured.<ref name="ap-f515e-rescue">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Kim |first=Seung Min |date=5 April 2026 |title=A Mountain Hideout and Aircraft Under Fire: US Carries out Daring Rescue of Service Member in Iran |url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-pilot-military-rescue-fde473d07fb59e871a71cd2ad2ffe4fe |access-date=6 April 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref>

On 6 April, the IRGC announced that the head of the IRGC's intelligence organisation, Major General [[Majid Khademi]], had been killed in a joint US-Israeli airstrike. Their statement claimed that Khademi had "played a major role in Iran's intelligence and security apparatus over nearly five decades".<ref name="ii-khademi">{{#invoke:cite |web |date=6 April 2026 |title=IRGC Intelligence Chief Killed in Attack, Guards Say |url=https://www.iranintl.com/en/202604065252 |access-date=6 April 2026 |website=[[Iran International]]}}</ref> Israel said that [[Yazdan Mir]], a high-ranking commander of the IRGC [[Quds Force]], had also been killed in the attacks.<ref name="6-4-toi-airstrikes">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Fabian |first=Emanuel |date=6 April 2026 |title=IDF Confirms Death of IRGC Intel Chief, Additional High-Ranking Officer in Overnight Strikes |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/idf-confirms-death-of-irgc-intel-chief-additional-high-ranking-officer-in-overnight-strikes/ |access-date=6 April 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref>

On the same day, before Trump's deadline for targeting Iranian infrastructure,<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/live/clyd9jddmprt |script-title=fa:ترامپ: تمام ایران را می‌توان در یک شب نابود کرد و آن ممکن است فردا شب باشد |title= |trans-title= |date=6 April 2026 |work=[[BBC News Persian]] |language=fa}}</ref> Israel carried out strikes on the South Pars Petrochemical facility in [[Asaluyeh]], Iran.<ref name="south-pars-waspo">{{#invoke:cite |news |date=6 April 2026 |title=Israel Hits Iran's South Pars Petrochemical Plant as Mediators Float New Ceasefire Proposal |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/04/06/iran-us-israel-trump-lebanon-april-6-2026/99367020-3176-11f1-b85b-2cd751275c1d_story.html |access-date=6 April 2026 |work=[[The Washington Post]] |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref> The IAF said that "85% of Iran's petrochemical exports" had been taken offline by now.<ref name="south-pars-toi">{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Fabian |first=Emanuel |date=6 April 2026 |title=Israel Says It Struck Iran's Largest Petrochemical Site |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/israel-says-it-struck-irans-largest-petrochemical-site/ |access-date=6 April 2026 |work=[[The Times of Israel]] |language=en-US |issn=0040-7909}}</ref>

At least 34 people, including six children, were killed in US-Israeli airstrikes across Iran, including against [[Sharif University of Technology]] and residential areas. Iranian vice president and reformist politician [[Mohammad Reza Aref]], who is also an alumnus of the university, described the alleged use of a [[bunker-buster bomb]] as a "symbol of Trump's madness and ignorance".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=6 April 2026 |title=Iran's Top University, Oil Facility Bombed as US, Israel Intensify Attacks |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/6/irans-top-university-bombed-as-us-israel-intensify-attacks-34-killed |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref>

[[File:Members of the Tehran Jewish community navigating the site where the Rafi'-Nia synagogue was destroyed.webm|thumb|Members of the Tehran Jewish community navigating the site where the Rafi'-Nia synagogue [[Destruction of the Rafi'-Nia synagogue|was destroyed]]]]
On 7 April, The Rafi'-Nia synagogue in central Tehran was [[Destruction of the Rafi'-Nia synagogue|destroyed in an airstrike]].<ref>{{cite news |date=7 April 2026 |title=Synagogue in Tehran 'Completely Destroyed' in US-Israeli Attack |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/7/synagogue-in-tehran-destroyed-in-us-israeli-strikes-on-iran |access-date=7 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |agency=[[Agence France Presse|AFP]] and [[Associated Press|AP]] |language=en}}</ref> Israel said that the building was destroyed due to collateral damage and that it was never meant to be the direct target of the airstrike.<ref name="Ynet070426">{{Cite news |last1=Ben Ari |first1=Lior |last2=Eichner |first2=Itamar |date=7 April 2026 |title=IDF Confirms Tehran Strike Targeted Iranian Commander, Synagogue Hit Was 'Collateral Damage' |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/jewish-world/article/sjouxfz211g |access-date=7 April 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref> The same day, US forces began strikes on [[Kharg Island]].<ref>{{cite news |date=7 April 2026 |title=US Strikes Military Targets on Iran's Kharg Island, US Official Says |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-strikes-military-targets-irans-kharg-island-us-official-says-2026-04-07/ |work=[[Reuters]] |access-date=7 April 2026}}</ref> In response, Iran said its restraint in targeting oil infrastructure in the region would no longer apply.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Maira |last=Butt |date=7 April 2026 |title=Kharg Island Targeted in Multiple Strikes as Iran Declares 'Restraint Is Over' |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news/iran-us-trump-kharg-island-oil-b2952970.html |access-date=11 April 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref> Trump posted to [[Truth Social]] that "{{anchor|WholeCivilizationDie}}a whole civilization will die tonight, never to be brought back again",<ref>{{cite news |last1=Svirnovskiy |first1=Gregory |title=Trump Threatens 'Whole Civilization Will Die Tonight' Ahead of Iran Deadline |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/07/trump-iran-deadline-threats-00861313 |access-date=7 April 2026 |work=[[Politico]] |date=7 April 2026 |language=en}}</ref> causing international concern that Trump would use nuclear weapons. The Secretary General of Amnesty International said that Trump's statement "may constitute a [[Incitement to genocide|threat to commit genocide]]".<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 April 2026 |title=Iran: President Trump's Apocalyptic Threats of Large-Scale Civilian Devastation Demand Urgent Global Action to Prevent Atrocity Crimes |url=https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/04/iran-president-trumps-apocalyptic-threats-of-large-scale-civilian-devastation-demand-urgent-global-action-to-prevent-atrocity-crimes/ |access-date=11 April 2026 |website=[[Amnesty International]] |language=en}}</ref> Multiple [[Right-wing politics|right-wing]] commentators and many Democrats condemned the post, and some [[Efforts to impeach Donald Trump|called for him to be removed]] through the [[Twenty-fifth Amendment to the United States Constitution|25th Amendment]].<ref name="Ferguson 2026">{{cite magazine |last1=Ferguson |first1=Malcolm |title=Trump's Former Allies Beg Someone to Learn the Nuke Codes to Stop Him |url=https://newrepublic.com/post/208714/trump-former-allies-nuclear-weapons-iran-25th-amendment |access-date=7 April 2026 |magazine=[[The New Republic]] |date=7 April 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=7 April 2026 |title=Trump Says 'A Whole Civilization Will Die Tonight' Ahead of Deadline for Iran |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/trump-threat-whole-civilization-will-die-iran-war-deadline-hormuz-rcna267059 |work=[[NBC News]] |access-date=7 April 2026}}</ref> The White House denied considering using nuclear weapons.<ref>{{cite news |date=7 April 2026 |title=Iran War Latest: We'll Destroy Iran — but We Won't Use Nuclear Weapons, US Says |url=https://www.thetimes.com/world/middle-east/article/iran-war-latest-news-tehran-rejects-peace-deadline-trump-gz662zx0h |work=[[The Times]] |access-date=7 April 2026}}</ref> The White House later said that "only the president knows" what he would do on Iran.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 April 2026 |title=White House Rules out Nuclear Weapons in Iran Amid Uncertainty over Peace Talks |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-rules-out-nuclear-weapons-in-iran-as-tehran-cuts-off-direct-diplomacy-with-washington-101775574170194.html |access-date=7 April 2026 |work=[[Hindustan Times]] |language=en}}</ref>

A leaked US intelligence report concluded that Iran retained 70% of missiles and launchers at this point, despite Trump [[False or misleading statements by Donald Trump (second term)#Claims about Iran|claims]] regarding "destruction" of Iran's military.<ref name="theguardian17july">{{cite news |last1=Sabbagh |first1=Dan |title=Iran proves it can still inflict damage despite waves of US attacks |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/17/iran-inflict-damage-us-attacks |work=The Guardian |date=17 July 2026}}</ref>

=== Ceasefire, dual blockade and Islamabad Memorandum (8 April – 19 June) ===
{{Main|2026 Iran war ceasefire|8 April 2026 Israeli attacks on Lebanon|Islamabad Talks|Islamabad Memorandum|2026 United States naval blockade of Iran|Operation Project Freedom}}

On 7 April, Trump announced that the US and Iran had reached [[2026 Iran war ceasefire|an agreement]] based on the 10-point proposal mediated by Pakistani prime minister [[Shehbaz Sharif]] and Field Marshal [[Asim Munir]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Live Updates: Trump Agrees to Two-Week Ceasefire After Threatening Massive Attacks |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/live-blog/live-updates-iran-war-trump-deadline-hormuz-infrastructure-ceasefire-rcna267039 |work=[[NBC News]] |date=7 April 2026 |access-date=8 April 2026}}</ref> The US, Israel, and Iran agreed to a two-week ceasefire, under which Iran would re-open the Strait of Hormuz.<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=What We Know About the US and Iran's Ceasefire Deal |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce84z6y3ke4o |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref>

After the announcement, Iran's [[Lavan Island]] oil refinery and [[Sirri Island]] crude export facilities [[2026 Lavan Island attack|were struck]]; no party claimed responsibility.<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=Iranian Oil Refining Company Confirms Attack on Lavan Refinery, Shana Reports |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/iranian-oil-refining-company-confirms-attack-lavan-refinery-shana-reports-2026-04-08/ |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> In response, Iran continued missile and drone strikes on Gulf Arab states.<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=S Arabia, UAE, Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain Report Attacks After Iran-US Truce |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/8/uae-kuwait-bahrain-report-attacks-despite-iran-us-ceasefire |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> The refinery attack was later revealed to have been done secretly by the UAE.<ref name="WSJUAEStrikes">{{Cite news |last1=Holliday |first1=Shelby |last2=Said |first2=Summer |date=11 May 2026 |title=The U.A.E. Has Been Secretly Carrying Out Attacks on Iran |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-u-a-e-has-been-secretly-carrying-out-attacks-on-iran-f1745a0d |access-date=11 May 2026 |work=Wall Street Journal |language=en-US |issn=0099-9660}}</ref><ref>Croft, Alex. [https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/middle-east/uae-military-strikes-iran-war-trump-b2974810.html 'UAE has secretly been carrying out military strikes on Iran, report says"], ''[[The Independent]]'', 12 May 2026. Accessed 12 May 2026.</ref><ref name=Telegraph20260512>White, Robert; Kelly, Kieran. [https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/05/12/uae-secret-attacks-on-iran/ "UAE and Saudi Arabia 'carried out secret attacks on Iran'"], ''[[The Daily Telegraph]]'', 12 May 2026. Accessed 12 May 2026.</ref>

[[File:8 April 2026 Isreali attacks on Beirut (2).jpg|thumb|right|Aftermath of [[8 April 2026 Lebanon attacks|8 April 2026 Israeli attacks]] on Beirut, Lebanon]]
Israel and the US asserted that the ceasefire did not include Lebanon,<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=Trump Says Lebanon Not Included in US-Iran Ceasefire Amid Israeli Assault |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/8/trump-says-lebanon-not-included-in-us-iran-ceasefire-amid-israeli-assault |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Brennan |first1=David |last2=Haworth |first2=Jon |last3=El-Bawab |first3=Nadine |date=9 April 2026 |title=Iran Live Updates: Iran Says Hormuz Is Open to All Ships That Coordinate with Tehran |url=https://abcnews.com/International/live-updates/iran-live-updates-casualties-reported-missile-strikes-israel/?id=131757074 |work=ABC |quote=Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said there is not a ceasefire in Lebanon in a recorded statement Thursday, saying strikes on Lebanon will resume.}}</ref> contradicting the Pakistani mediators and Iran.<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=Netanyahu Says US-Iran Ceasefire 'Does Not Include Lebanon' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/8/netanyahu-says-us-iran-ceasefire-does-not-include-lebanon |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> Hezbollah said it had halted attacks on Israel and on Israeli soldiers in Lebanon.<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=Hezbollah Pauses Attacks Under US-Iran Ceasefire, Sources Close to Group Say |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/hezbollah-pauses-attacks-under-us-iran-ceasefire-sources-close-group-say-2026-04-08/ |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Reuters]] |language=en}}</ref> Despite the ceasefire, Israel launched "[[April 8, 2026 Lebanon attacks|Operation Eternal Darkness]]", which, according to Israeli forces, included targeting all Hezbollah's command and control centers in southern Lebanon, [[Beirut]] and the [[Beqaa Valley]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Krisi |first=Ron |date=8 April 2026 |title=IDF: We Launched Operation 'Eternal Darkness' in Lebanon; Working Assumption - Fighting with Iran Will Resume |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/buf6bj7sg |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref> Local observers disputed this, saying the attacks were not targeted.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/lebanon/lebanon-israel-attack-iran-ceasefire-hezbollah-rcna267260|title=Israel launches sprawling attacks on Lebanon after Iran ceasefire was declared|website=[[NBC News]]|date=8 April 2026}}</ref> These were the largest attacks since the start of the war,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Israel Pounds Lebanon with Heaviest Airstrikes of the War as Hezbollah Pauses Attacks |date=8 April 2026 |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Reuters]] |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/hezbollah-pauses-attacks-under-us-iran-ceasefire-sources-close-group-say-2026-04-08/}}</ref> killing at least 357 people and injuring more than 1,200.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 April 2026 |title=Lebanon Says Death Toll from Israeli Strikes on Wednesday Rises to 357 |url=https://arab.news/9k322 |access-date=14 April 2026 |website=Arab News |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=Israeli Attacks Across Lebanon Kill at Least 254 After Iran-US Ceasefire |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/8/hundreds-of-casualties-across-lebanon-after-israel-says-it-hit-100-sites |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en}}</ref> In Beirut alone, 92 people were killed and at least 740 injured.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 April 2026 |title=Large-Scale Israeli Strikes Hit Beirut, Lebanese Areas Despite U.S.-Iran Truce |url=https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2026/04/08/Lebanon-Israel-strikes-Beirut/9641775655878/ |access-date=8 April 2026 |website=[[United Press International]] |language=en}}</ref> In response, Iran threatened to attack Israel "if the aggressions against dear Lebanon are not brought to an immediate end".<ref>{{Cite news |date=8 April 2026 |title=Iran's IRGC Warns of 'Regret-Inducing Response' If Attacks on Lebanon Continue - State Media |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c5yw4g3z7qgt?post=asset%3Afe928469-1710-40e4-b894-1c1661ed4e9c#post |access-date=8 April 2026 |work=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> Iran paused Hormuz traffic over Israeli attacks in Lebanon.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://g1.globo.com/mundo/noticia/2026/04/08/ira-ameaca-romper-cessar-fogo-se-israel-continuar-atacando-o-libano.ghtml |title=Irã Ameaça Romper Cessar-Fogo Se Israel Continuar Atacando O Líbano |first=Artur |last=Alvarez |date=8 April 2026 |website=G1 |language=pt-BR}}</ref> Hezbollah claimed responsibility for launching rockets towards northern Israel as a response to "ceasefire violations".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=9 April 2026 |title=Hezbollah: Rockets Fired at Northern Israel in Response to 'Cease-Fire Violations' |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-04-09/ty-article-live/hezbollah-says-it-fired-rockets-at-israel-in-response-to-cease-fire-violations/0000019d-6fff-d68a-a39d-6fff46d70000 |access-date=9 April 2026 |work=[[Haaretz]]}}</ref>

On 11 April, Trump said that American forces had started "[[2026 Strait of Hormuz campaign|clearing]]" the Strait of Hormuz.<ref>{{Cite news |date=11 April 2026 |title=Trump Says U.S. Forces Are 'Clearing' Strait of Hormuz |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-strait-of-hormuz-clearing-empty-tankers-heading-to-us-to-load-up-with-oil-and-gas/article70850847.ece |access-date=11 April 2026 |agency=[[Reuters]] |work=[[The Hindu]] |language=en-IN |issn=0971-751X}}</ref> Iran claimed that an American ship on its way to the strait turned back after being warned.<ref>{{Cite news |date=11 April 2026 |title=US Military Ship Turns Back from Hormuz Route After Iran's 30-Min Warning |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-military-ship-turns-back-from-hormuz-route-after-irans-30-min-warning-101775915292475.html |access-date= |work=[[Hindustan Times]] |language=en |last=Alam |first=Majid}}</ref> ''[[The Wall Street Journal]]'' reported US Navy [[destroyer]]s entered the strait for the first time since the war began. The Iranian government reportedly threatened to attack the ships, accusing the US of a ceasefire violation.<ref>{{Cite news |date=11 April 2026 |title=U.S. Warships Transit Hormuz as U.S.-Iran Meet Face-To-Face For Peace Talks |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-war-latest-news-israel-us-lebanon-2026?mod=lc_navigation |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Ravid |first=Barak |date=11 April 2026 |title=U.S. Warships Cross Strait of Hormuz for First Time Since Iran War Began |url=https://www.axios.com/2026/04/11/us-iran-navy-strait-of-hormuz |website=[[Axios (website)|Axios]] |language=en}}</ref> [[United States Central Command|US Central Command]] said the ships were [[minesweeping]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=11 April 2026 |title=US Military 'Setting Conditions' to Clear Mines from Strait of Hormuz |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/trump-says-us-forces-are-clearing-strait-hormuz-2026-04-11/ |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> On the same day, the [[Islamabad Talks|talks between the US and Iran]]—the highest-level discussions between the two since the [[1979 Islamic Revolution]]—were held in [[Islamabad]], Pakistan, lasting 21 hours. [[JD Vance]] announced no agreement was reached and Iran had refused "to accept our terms".<ref>{{Cite news |date=12 April 2026 |title=No Deal: U.S.-Iran Peace Talks in Islamabad Collapse |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/04/12/nx-s1-5782538/u-s-iran-peace-talks-islamabad-collapse |access-date= |work=[[NPR News]] |language=en}}</ref> Trump stated he no longer cared about negotiations.<ref>{{cite news |title=Trump Says He 'Doesn't Care' If Iran Returns to Peace Talks After Islamabad Negotiations Collapse |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/trump-iran-peace-pakistan-negotiations-b2956495.html |work=[[The Independent]] |date=13 April 2026}}</ref>

Trump declared that the US Navy would begin [[2026 United States naval blockade of Iran|its blockade]] of "all Ships trying to enter, or leave, the Strait of Hormuz" from 13 April. He said the US Navy would stop any ships that paid tolls to Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:Cite |web |date=12 April 2026 |title=Trump Says U.S. Will Blockade Strait of Hormuz and Intercept Ships That Paid Tolls to Iran |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-strait-of-hormuz-blockade-iran/ |access-date=12 April 2026 |website=CBS News |language=en-US}}</ref> However, [[United States Central Command]] clarified that the blockade would only be enforced on ships travelling to or from Iranian ports.<ref>{{#invoke:Cite |news |date=12 April 2026 |title=Trump Announces Naval Blockade of Iran After Islamabad Talks Yield No Deal |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/04/12/iran-us-talks-ceasefire-vance/ |access-date=13 April 2026 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref> The [[Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps Navy|IRGC Navy]] said any military vessel approaching the strait would be considered a ceasefire violation and meet a "severe response."<ref>{{#invoke:Cite |news |date=12 April 2026 |title=Update by Parin Behrooz |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/12/world/iran-war-trump-talks-pakistan/d43e91d7-9511-5fb7-b3de-26e6da723f33?smid=url-share |access-date=12 April 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Trump threatened to strike fast-attack ships of the IRGC Navy, similar to [[United States strikes on alleged drug traffickers during Operation Southern Spear|US strikes on drug traffickers during Operation Southern Spear]].<ref>{{#invoke:Cite |news |last=De Avila|first=Joseph |date=13 April 2026|title=Trump Threatens Iranian Ships with Drug-Boat-Style Strikes |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-us-cease-fire-talks-stalled-2026/card/amH2Xp6TKrmqVi1IOeEQ |access-date=13 April 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Iran had 13 days of oil storage capacity, forcing it to shut down its oil fields and potentially damaging them.<ref name="SleimanISW2026_04_14">{{#invoke:Cite |web |last=Sleiman |first=Nadia |date=14 April 2026 |title=Iran Update Special Report, April 13, 2026 |url=https://understandingwar.org/research/middle-east/iran-update-special-report-april-13-2026/ |access-date=14 April 2026 |website=[[Institute for the Study of War]] |language=en-US}}</ref> An analyst estimated loss of import and export capacity would be US$435 million per day.<ref name="SleimanISW2026_04_14" />

On 16 April, Trump announced that Israel and Lebanon agreed to [[2026 Israel–Lebanon ceasefire|a ten-day truce]].<ref>{{#invoke:Cite|news |date=16 April 2026 |title=Trump Says Israel and Lebanon Agree to Temporary Ceasefire|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/16/trump-says-israel-and-lebanon-agree-to-temporary-ceasefire |access-date=16 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref> Iran announced that passage of commercial vessels through the strait would be allowed during the truce.<ref>{{#invoke:Cite|news |date=17 April 2026 |title=Iran's Foreign Minister Says Passage of Vessels via Hormuz Strait Is Open During Ceasefire |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/irans-foreign-minister-says-passage-vessels-via-hormuz-strait-is-open-during-2026-04-17/ |access-date=17 April 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> Despite this, Trump said that the blockade would continue,<ref>{{#invoke:Cite |news |date=17 April 2026 |title=Trump Says Blockade on Iran 'In Full Force' Until Deal Is Reached |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/trump-says-blockade-iran-in-full-force-until-deal-is-reached-2026-04-17/ |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> so Iran announced it would reimpose restrictions on the strait.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/world/2026/04/17/iran-war-ceasefire-lebanon-trump-updates--live/89652291007/ |title=Strait of Hormuz Won't Reopen, Iranian Leader Tells Trump |first1=Michael |last1=Loria |first2=Christopher |last2=Cann |first3=Andrea |last3=Riquier |work=[[USA Today]] |date=17 April 2026 |access-date=18 April 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2026/04/17/iran-trump-strait-hormuz-oil-tanker-traffic.html |title=Video Shows Ships Turning Away from the Strait of Hormuz as Confusion Persists over Whether Sea Lane Is Really Open |first=Spencer |last=Kendall |work=[[CNBC]] |date=17 April 2026 |access-date=18 April 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:Cite|web|date=18 April 2026 |title=Iran Reimposes Restrictions on Hormuz, Accuses US of Violating Deal|url=https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/iran-reimposes-restrictions-on-hormuz-accuses-us-of-violating-deal-126041800390_1.html |access-date=18 April 2026 |agency=[[Associated Press]]|website=Business Standard}}</ref> The US stated that its blockade had intercepted 23 ships.<!-- per [[WP:SOCIALMEDIA]] as this is a claim about themselves and not particularly unbelievable, a primary source links to the social media announcement from a verified government agency is acceptable --><ref>{{#invoke:Cite tweet | |user=CENTCOM |number=2045464604688384243 |title=Littoral Combat Ship USS Canberra (LCS 30) Patrols the Arabian Sea During the U.S. Blockade |date=18 April 2026}}</ref>

Despite Iran's seizure of two cargo ships,<ref name="Guardian 24 Apr 26">{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Trump Claims US Has Total Control over Strait of Hormuz After Iran Seizes Two Container Ships |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/23/trump-claims-us-has-total-control-over-strait-of-hormuz-as-iran-seizes-two-container-ships |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=24 April 2026}}</ref> Trump claimed total control over the strait.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Trump Says He Is Keeping Strait of Hormuz Closed, Not Iran |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/video/newsfeed/2026/4/23/trump-says-he-is-keeping-strait-of-hormuz-closed-not-iran |work=[[Al Jazeera English]] |date=23 April 2026}}</ref> ''[[The Guardian]]'' described the situation as a "dual blockade", saying that while the US Navy could blockade Iranian ports, it had been unable to stop Iran's blockade and open the strait to allies.<ref name="Guardian 24 Apr 26" /> Israel and Lebanon agreed a three-week extension of their ceasefire.<ref>{{#invoke:Cite |news |date=23 April 2026 |title=Iran War Updates: Trump Announces Three-Week Lebanon Ceasefire Extension |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/23/iran-war-live-israel-kills-lebanese-journalist-tehran-us-talks-stalled |access-date=24 April 2026 |work=[[Al Jazeera English]]}}</ref>

On 8 June, the IDF announced that it struck military sites in Iran, with explosions reported in Tehran, Isfahan, and Tabriz.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/trump-says-new-israel-iran-strikes-wont-affect-peace-deal-2026-06-08/|title=Israel Hits Iran with New Strikes Despite Trump Admonition|website=Reuters|date=8 June 2026}}</ref> This triggered an exchange between the two countries.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.springfieldnewssun.com/nation-world/israel-and-iran-trade-strikes-threatening-to-drag-the-region-back-into-full-scale-war/article_88e67032-7cf2-5ce8-803a-218d9bcb78a4.html|title=Israel and Iran Trade Strikes, Threatening to Drag the Region Back into Full-Scale War|agency=Associated Press|website=Springfield News-Sun|date=8 June 2026}}</ref> Two Iranian soldiers were killed in an Israeli attack.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.millenniumpost.in/world/at-least-2-iranian-military-members-killed-in-israeli-attack-on-iran-663595|title=At Least 2 Iranian Military Members Killed in Israeli Attack on Iran|website=Millenniumpost |date=9 June 2026}}</ref> Iran afterwards said it had ceased military actions against Israel.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/west-asia-conflict-iran-us-israel-war-beirut-strikes-strait-of-hormuz-live-updates-june-8-2026/article71074947.ece|title=West Asia War LIVE: Iran Ends Military Operations Against Israel, Warns of Harsher Attacks If Strikes on Lebanon Persist|website=[[The Hindu]]|date=8 June 2026}}</ref> Israel stopped strikes at Trump's request.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/iran-fires-missiles-at-israel-after-israeli-airstrike-on-beirut-a93b4da7|title=Iran and Israel Halt Exchanges of Fire|website=The Wall Street Journal|date=8 June 2026}}</ref>

On 9 June, ''The New York Times'' reported that American crew was rescued after a helicopter went down near the strait. CENTCOM said they were rescued by a US Navy [[Unmanned surface vehicle|drone boat]] for the first time.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/crew-rescued-after-us-helicopter-goes-down-near-strait-hormuz-nyt-reports-2026-06-09/|title=Trump Says Pilots Safe After US Army Apache Goes Down Near Hormuz|website=Reuters|date=9 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/apache-helicopter-crash-coast-oman-4de26c6d|title=Drone Boat Rescues Crew of Downed U.S. Apache Helicopter Near Hormuz|website=The Wall Street Journal|date=9 June 2026}}</ref><ref name="reuters9june">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us-military-says-it-began-launching-strikes-against-iran-2026-06-09/|title=US Military Launches New Strikes on Iran After Apache Downing|website=Reuters|date=9 June 2026}}</ref> Trump said Iranians had shot down the helicopter and pledged to respond.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/6/9/trump-says-iran-shot-down-us-helicopters-over-hormuz-vows-to-respond|title=Trump Says Iran Shot Down US Helicopter over Hormuz, Vows to Respond|website=Al Jazeera English|date=9 June 2026}}</ref> A US official said a [[Shahed drones|Shahed one-way attack drone]] downed the helicopter.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/06/09/world/iran-war-trump-israel-lebanon/9bf1b8f1-9257-53d1-8a59-fefdb79ff421?smid=url-share|title=Iran War Live|quote=A one-way Iranian Shahed attack drone downed the Apache helicopter gunship on Monday, a U.S. official said on Tuesday, confirming an earlier report by Axios. President Trump had announced earlier on social media that Iran had shot down the helicopter as it patrolled near the Strait of Hormuz, but he did not provide details.|website=The New York Times|date=9 June 2026}}</ref> Iran said it did not deliberately target the helicopter.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/6/9/iran-war-live-trump-warns-netanyahu-as-israel-tehran-halt?update=4641192|title=Iran's Deputy FM Says Country Did Not Deliberately Target US Helicopter|website=Al Jazeera English|date=9 June 2026}}</ref> CENTCOM later said that it launched "self-defense" strikes in retaliation.<ref name="reuters9june"/> One attack damaged [[Water tank|water reservoir tanks]] in [[Bandar Sirik|Sirik]]; Iran stated that 20,000 people had lost access to drinking water.<ref name="GhaffariFT2026_06_09">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.ft.com/content/155db8a4-f2ff-463b-9c6c-2b1a8104750c?syn-25a6b1a6=1|title=Iran Says 20,000 People Left Without Water After US Hits Reservoir Tanks|website=[[The Financial Times]]|date=9 June 2026|archive-date=10 June 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260610163413/https://www.ft.com/content/155db8a4-f2ff-463b-9c6c-2b1a8104750c?syn-25a6b1a6=1|url-status=live|last=Ghaffari|first=Bita|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3356630/thousands-iranians-left-without-water-searing-heat-after-us-hits-reservoirs|title=US Destroys Iran Reservoirs, Leaving Thousands Without Water in Searing Heat|website=South China Morning Post|agency=Agence France-Presse|date=10 June 2026}}</ref>

On 14 June, Iran said that the draft US deal included Tehran agreeing not to produce or acquire nuclear weapons, and the US agreeing to allow Tehran to dilute its highly enriched uranium stockpile in Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-says-draft-us-deal-includes-oil-sanctions-waiver-nuclear-limits-and-asset-release|title=Iran Says Draft US Deal Includes Oil Sanctions Waiver, Nuclear Limits and Asset Release|agency=Reuters|website=The Straits Times|date=14 June 2026}}</ref> Trump and Iran announced they had reached an agreement to end the war and reopen the strait. Trump said he had authorized the lifting of the US blockade.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |url=https://www.standard-democrat.com/world/qatari-mediators-travel-to-tehran-for-final-touches-on-a-possible-deal-to-end-war-8507ea74 |title=A Tentative Deal Is Reached to End the Iran War and Trump Orders a Stop to the US Naval Blockade |agency=Associated Press |date=14 June 2026 |website=Standard Democrat |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260617205150/https://www.standard-democrat.com/world/qatari-mediators-travel-to-tehran-for-final-touches-on-a-possible-deal-to-end-war-8507ea74 |archive-date=17 June 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 15 June, US vice president [[JD Vance]] announced that the memorandum was digitally signed by both countries the previous day.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.wionews.com/world/vance-says-us-iran-mou-was-signed-digitally-before-planned-switzerland-meeting-1781541865091|title=Vance Says US-Iran MoU Was Signed Digitally Before Planned Switzerland Meeting|website=Wion|date=15 June 2026}}</ref> On 17 June, Trump and Iranian president [[Masoud Pezeshkian]] signed the memorandum of understanding to end the war, with Trump signing it during dinner with French president [[Emmanuel Macron]] at the [[Palace of Versailles]] after the [[52nd G7 summit|G7 summit]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.deccanchronicle.com/world/iran-mou-signed-on-wednesday-by-trump-iran-president-us-official-1964365|title=Trump, Iran's President Sign Deal To End West Asia War|agency=Agence France Presse|website=Deccan Chronicle|date=17 June 2026}}</ref> On 18 June, Pakistan stated that the signing of the memorandum implies Tehran will reopen the Hormuz "instantly" and the American blockade will end "immediately."<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-to-instantly-reopen-hormuz-us-to-immediately-lift-blockade-pak-pm-shehbaz-sharif-11652070|title=Iran To "Instantly" Reopen Hormuz, US To "Immediately" Lift Blockade: Pak PM|agency=Agence France Presse|website=NDTV|date=18 June 2026}}</ref> CENTCOM announced that it had removed the naval blockade.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/6/18/us-military-says-it-has-lifted-naval-blockade-of-iranian-ports|title=US Military Says It Has Lifted Naval Blockade of Iranian Ports|website=Al Jazeera English|date=18 June 2026}}</ref>

On 19 June, Trump announced a renewed ceasefire between Israel and [[Hezbollah]] in the [[2026 Lebanon war]], facilitated by the US, Qatar, and Iran.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.ndtvprofit.com/world/trump-envoy-heads-to-switzerland-for-potential-us-iran-talks-after-lebanon-ceasefire-what-to-expect-11662093|title=Trump Envoy Heads To Switzerland For Potential US-Iran Talks After Lebanon Ceasefire: What To Expect?|website=[[NDTV Profit]]|date=20 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.wionews.com/world/israel-and-hezbollah-agree-to-ceasefire-starting-friday-after-latest-flare-up-says-report-citing-us-official-1781877376072|title=Israel and Hezbollah agree to ceasefire starting Friday after latest flare-up, says report citing US official|website=[[Wion]]|date=19 June 2026}}</ref> Hezbollah announced an attack on Israeli forces trying to capture Ali al-Taher in [[Nabatieh]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://aje.news/o3j66i?update=4682113|title='Devastating Day': Ceasefire in Lebanon Is One in Name Only|website=[[Al Jazeera English]]|date=20 June 2026}}</ref> Israel continued to strike southern Lebanon numerous times.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://aje.news/cllifw?update=4678945|title=Southern Lebanon Hit by at Least 12 Israeli Strikes Since Ceasefire|website=Al Jazeera English|date=19 June 2026}}</ref>

=== Renewed hostilities (8 July – present) ===
{{Main|Timeline of the 2026 Iran war|July 2026 United States strikes against Iran|2026 Damietta drone strike}}
On 8 July, Trump declared the MOU was "over", adding that he lacked further desire to deal with Iran's leadership, after Iran allegedly struck more targets in the Strait of Hormuz.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/sjyyiyoxze|title=Trump says Iran deal 'is over' after Gulf strikes, calls Tehran 'sick people'|website=[[Ynet]]|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> Trump later stated that US negotiators could continue negotiations, although he expressed pessimism about the outcome.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://english.aawsat.com/world/5293567-trump-says-ceasefire-iran-over-negotiations-can-continue|title=Trump Warns Iran That US Is Preparing for More Strikes After Saying Ceasefire Is Over|work=[[Asharq Al-Awsat]]|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> Iranian state media announced that eight soldiers were killed in American attacks in ⁠[[Bandar Abbas]] and [[Bushehr]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-08/ty-article-live/u-s-launches-retaliatory-strikes-against-iran-hitting-more-than-80-targets/0000019f-3f72-d913-abff-bf7a77a60000?liveBlogItemId=656905481#656905481|title=Eight Iranian soldiers killed in U.S. strikes, state media says|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> Trump added that the war would not resume, but if it did, it would be short, that he might be assassinated by Iran, and he was the top target on Iran's hit list.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/trump-war-with-iran-not-starting-up-again-but-if-it-does-itll-be-quick/|title=Trump: War with Iran not starting up again, but if it does, it'll be quick|website=The Times of Israel|date=8 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/trump-qatari-gifted-air-force-one-to-be-brought-to-us-bases-in-europe-so-troops-can-marvel-at-it/|title=Trump: Qatari-gifted Air Force One to be brought to US bases in Europe so troops can marvel at it|website=The Times of Israel|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> [[Mehr News Agency]] reported that the US attacks killed two Iranian fishermen.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-08/ty-article-live/u-s-launches-retaliatory-strikes-against-iran-hitting-more-than-80-targets/0000019f-3f72-d913-abff-bf7a77a60000?liveBlogItemId=1318123296#1318123296|title=Two Iranian fishermen killed in U.S. strikes, Mehr News Agency says|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> CENTCOM announced that it hit roughly 90 Iranian military targets, including air defense systems, coastal surveillance assets, missile and drone storage facilities, naval capabilities, and military logistics infrastructure along the country's coastline.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-09/ty-article-live/u-s-strikes-targets-in-iran-for-second-night-in-a-row/0000019f-449e-d269-af9f-46df98160000?liveBlogItemId=232655488#232655488|title=CENTCOM: U.S. forces attacked 90 targets in Iran, including air defenses and missile and drone sites|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=9 July 2026}}</ref> [[Islamic Republic News Agency|IRNA]] reported that a US attack hit an airport in southeastern Iran, killing a fireman.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-08/ty-article-live/u-s-launches-retaliatory-strikes-against-iran-hitting-more-than-80-targets/0000019f-3f72-d913-abff-bf7a77a60000?liveBlogItemId=1308912639#1308912639|title=Fireman killed after attack on airport in southeastern Iran, IRNA reports|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> On 10 July, ''The Wall Street Journal'' reported that Israel provided intelligence with the US on a new [[Alleged Iranian plot to assassinate Donald Trump|conspiracy by the Iranian regime to assassinate Donald Trump]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/iran-hatched-fresh-plot-to-kill-trump-israel-told-u-s-1511d9d2?st=gvUrbi&reflink=desktopwebshare_permalink|title=Iran Hatched Fresh Plot to Kill Trump, Israel Told U.S.|website=The Wall Street Journal|date=10 July 2026}}</ref> Trump refuted the claim, stating, "I've left instructions—if anything happens, to literally bomb them at levels that they've never seen before."<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/trump-denies-that-israel-passed-on-intel-about-iranian-plot-to-assassinate-him/|title=Trump denies that Israel passed on intel about Iranian plot to assassinate him|website=The Times of Israel|date=10 July 2026}}</ref>

The administrative council of the [[International Maritime Organization]] (IMO) agreed that member states should reject Iranian efforts to ‌impose sovereignty over the Hormuz and Tehran's "unilateral decision" to form a body to control traffic on the waterway.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/countries-must-reject-iran-efforts-control-hormuz-un-agency-document-says-2026-07-10/|title=Countries must reject Iran efforts to control Hormuz, UN agency document says|website=Reuters|date=10 July 2026}}</ref> The IRGC's navy said it closed the strait until further notice after firing a warning shot at a vessel trying to transit through an unapproved route.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-11/ty-article-live/aoc-calls-to-release-gaza-hospital-director-hussam-abu-safiya/0000019f-4de2-d38b-afbf-5ff684110004?liveBlogItemId=785550510#785550510|title=Iran says Strait of Hormuz is closed, claims it struck vessel using 'unauthorized route'|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=11 July 2026}}</ref> On 13 July, Trump announced that the US will reinstate the "Iranian blockade in the Strait" and impose a 20% toll on cargo shipping through it.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-13/ty-article-live/one-killed-four-wounded-in-u-s-strike-in-southwestern-iran-state-media-says/0000019f-591e-de66-a5bf-5b5f62030000?liveBlogItemId=859504089#859504089|title=Trump: U.S. 'reinstating the Iranian blockade' in Strait of Hormuz|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=13 July 2026}}</ref> The Yemeni government and Saudi Arabia struck the [[Sanaa International Airport]] controlled by the Houthis,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/13/yemen-govt-says-its-forces-attacked-sanaa-airport|title=Tension rising as Yemen gov't attacks Sanaa airport, Houthis fire missiles|website=Al Jazeera English|date=13 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.internazionale.it/ultime-notizie-reuters/2026/07/13/yemeni-military-targets-sanaa-airport-runway-to-stop-iranian-plane-landing-defence-ministry-says|title=Houthis fire missiles at Saudi Arabia, breaking years of calm|work=[[Internazionale (magazine)|Internazionale]]|date=13 July 2026}}</ref> allegedly to prevent an Iranian plane from landing.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/yemen/yemen-saudi-arabia-air-strike-sanna-airport-houthi-rebels-rcna587273|title=Saudi Arabian airstrikes hit Sanaa International Airport, Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen say|website=NBC News|date=13 July 2026}}</ref> The Houthis retaliated by launching missiles and drones against Saudi Arabia's [[Abha International Airport]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/07/13/yemen-rebels-announce-end-of-de-escalation-phase-after-sanaa-airport-strikes/|title=Houthis fire missiles at Saudi Arabia after blast at Sanaa airport|website=The National|date=13 July 2026|last=Mostafa|first=Amr}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://aje.news/9m5azt?update=4767151|title=Houthis claim to target Saudi Arabia's Abha airport|website=[[Al Jazeera English]]|date=13 July 2026}}</ref> The [[Combined Maritime Forces]]' Joint Maritime Information Centre (JMIC), led by America, announced that the US blockade on Iran would start the following day.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-13/ty-article-live/one-killed-four-wounded-in-u-s-strike-in-southwestern-iran-state-media-says/0000019f-591e-de66-a5bf-5b5f62030000?liveBlogItemId=1363693602#1363693602|title=U.S. naval blockade of Iran to begin Tuesday, maritime security information center says|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=13 July 2026}}</ref> The US announced that it hit military targets throughout Iran including Bushehr, [[Chabahar]], [[Jask]], [[Konarak, Iran|Konarak]], [[Abu Musa]], and Bandar Abbas.{{efn|Abu Musa island is currently under Iranian governance, but the UAE dispute its sovereignty.<ref name="estimate">{{cite news |url=http://www.theestimate.com/public/072401.html |title=Abu Musa and The Tumbs: The Dispute That Won't Go Away, Part Two |date=24 July 2001 |work=The Estimate |volume=XIII |issue=13 |access-date=14 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071215021736/http://www.theestimate.com/public/072401.html |archive-date=15 December 2007 |url-status=unfit}}</ref><ref name="wi">{{cite web |last=Henderson |first=Simon |url=https://www.washingtoninstitute.org/policy-analysis/unwanted-guest-gulf-summit-and-iran |title=Unwanted Guest: The Gulf Summit and Iran |date=7 December 2007 |access-date=14 July 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210123084614/https://www.washingtoninstitute.org/policy-analysis/unwanted-guest-gulf-summit-and-iran |archive-date=23 January 2021 |url-status=live}}</ref>}}<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-14/ty-article-live/idf-detains-several-israelis-who-attempted-to-cross-border-into-syria/0000019f-5e52-d72f-afff-5f7e97fc0000?liveBlogItemId=2036813987#2036813987|title=U.S. says it has completed latest wave of strikes on Iran|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=14 July 2026}}</ref> Two Emirati tankers were reportedly struck by Iranian cruise missiles in the strait in Oman's territorial waters, killing one Indian crew member and injuring two critically.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-13/ty-article-live/one-killed-four-wounded-in-u-s-strike-in-southwestern-iran-state-media-says/0000019f-591e-de66-a5bf-5b5f62030000?liveBlogItemId=880999897#880999897|title=UAE says two tankers hit by Iranian cruise missiles in Strait of Hormuz; one crew member killed|agency=[[Reuters]]|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=14 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/india/india-protests-iran-over-killing-seafarer-hormuz-2026-07-14/|title=India protests to Iran over killing of seafarer in Hormuz|website=Reuters|date=14 July 2026}}</ref> On 14 July, Trump cancelled plans to impose fees in the strait.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-hormuz-strait-war-july-14-2026-abd060c55feea216625689e57d8f76be|title=Trump backs away from plans to charge fees in the Strait of Hormuz as attacks intensify|website=Associated Press|date=14 July 2026}}</ref> The IMO said that the death toll from Hormuz ship attacks on that day increased to two.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nampa.org/text/22967142|title=London, July 14, 2026 (AFP) - Death toll in latest Hormuz vessel strikes rises to two: maritime group|agency=Agence France Presse|website=Namibia Press Agency|date=15 July 2026}}</ref>

On 20 July, the Houthis declared a blockade of Saudi Arabian ports and ships in the [[Bab-el-Mandeb]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/7/23/how-shipping-insurance-rates-are-rising-as-hormuz-bab-al-mandeb-shut-down|title=How shipping insurance rates are rising, as Hormuz, Bab al-Mandeb shut down|website=[[Al Jazeera English]]|date=23 July 2026}}</ref> a strait connecting the Red Sea to the Indian Ocean. On 1 August, ''[[The New York Times]]'' reported, citing state and local officials, that evidence leads to Iran in a series of cyberattacks against water systems in at least seven US states, with [[Michigan]] being the second state to report the attacks publicly.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/01/us/politics/iran-cyberattack-water-systems.html|title=Scope of Hacks on U.S. Water Supply Widens as Evidence Points to Iran|website=[[The New York Times]]|date=1 August 2026}}</ref> 

[[BBC Verify]] found new damages to nine American military bases between 12 July and 1 August, according to satellite images. Targets with verified damages include [[Muwaffaq Salti Air Base]], Tower 22 base (the site of [[Tower 22 drone attack|a deadly attack in 2024]]), Isa Air Base, [[Erbil Air Base]], and [[Mina Abdullah Refinery]]. According to [[Farzin Nadimi]], a Senior Fellow with [[The Washington Institute for Near East Policy|The Washington Institute]], the Iranian attacks in the renewed conflict since 12 July have been "more extensive and more effective", with support from [[Russia in the 2026 Iran war|Russia]] and [[China in the 2026 Iran war|China]] in the form of satellite imagery to target American forces and assess damage.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.bbc.com/persian/articles/c70gxky16wxo|title=تحقیقات بی‌بی‌سی: شواهد تازه از خسارت به مراکز آمریکایی هدف حملات ایران در خلیج فارس و اردن|website=[[BBC Persian]]|date=1 August 2026|language=fa}}</ref> Major General Ali Abdollahi, the commander of Iran’s military forces, stated that the United States is conducting a comprehensive military campaign throughout the entire region with escalating intensity. He further asserted that the United States is utilizing the capitals and infrastructure of Arab nations to safeguard its strategic interests.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Motamedi |first1=Maziar |title=Iran warns against 'flames of war' amid US strike threats on energy sites |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/1/iran-warns-against-fire-of-war-amid-us-strike-threats-on-energy-sites |website=[[Al Jazeera English]] |date=1 August 2026}}</ref>

On 2 August, after [[Qatar as a mediator in conflict|Qatari efforts to head off the attacks and open the Hormuz]] and Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman expressed concern about Trump's plans for massive strikes on Iran,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/israel-was-supposed-to-be-part-of-iran-strike-us-official/|title='Israel was supposed to be part of Iran strike' — US official|website=[[The Times of Israel]]|date=2 August 2026}}</ref> Trump stated that he and Israel had called off the attack after the Iranian regime requested more time for a deal, and that a plan was in place for US forces to carry out the largest US operation since [[World War II]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.usnews.com/news/politics/articles/2026-08-03/iran-deja-vu-trump-once-again-threatens-massive-escalation-against-tehran-only-to-walk-back|title=Trump Says New Talks Are 'Last Chance' for Iran to Forge Deal and Avoid Escalation of US Strikes|agency=Associated Press|website=[[U.S. News & World Report]]|date=3 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.axios.com/2026/08/01/saudi-crown-prince-trump-iran-attacks|title=Scoop: MBS raises concerns over Trump's plans for massive Iran strikes|website=[[Axios (website)|Axios]]|date=1 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/us-news/2026-08-02/ty-article/.premium/trump-says-he-canceled-iran-attack-after-tehran-sought-more-time-for-deal/0000019f-c052-d37f-adff-d5fe01a30000|title=Trump Says He Canceled Iran Attack After Tehran Sought More Time for Deal|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=2 August 2026}}</ref> The [[Islamic Republic of Iran Armed Forces]] denied requesting the US to halt strikes, calling Trump's claim a "lie".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-08-02/ty-article-live/reports-six-killed-including-a-child-in-a-wave-of-israeli-strikes-across-gaza/0000019f-c01e-de7a-afff-cf9eab5d0000?liveBlogItemId=521736306#521736306|title=Iranian military sources deny asking U.S. to halt strikes, call Trump's claim 'a lie'|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=2 August 2026}}</ref> 

On 3 August, Iran stated that there were not currently negotiating with the Americans, denying Trump's claims that negotiations with Iran would start that day.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/iran-says-no-current-talks-with-us-2026-08-03/|title=Iran says no current talks with U.S.|website=[[Reuters]]|date=3 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/iran-says-no-talks-with-us-on-hormuz-deal-with-oman-wont-open-strait/|title=Iran says no talks with US on Hormuz, deal with Oman won't open strait|website=[[The Times of Israel]]|date=3 August 2026}}</ref> Iran is in talks with Oman, but the agreement is not enough to open the Strait of Hormuz, according to Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmail Baghaei.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/trump-iran-talks-attacks-canceled-hormuz-nuclear-rcna590535|title=Trump says new Iran talks will start Monday after calling off attacks|website=[[NBC News]]|date=3 August 2026}}</ref>
Trump set a deadline of the following day for a deal with Iran and threatened "[[Decapitation (military strategy)|decapitation]]".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-08-04/ty-article-live/as-board-of-peace-urges-de-escalation-idf-strikes-reportedly-kill-two-in-gaza/0000019f-ca64-db33-a5ff-fa7420cf0000?liveBlogItemId=1984052610#1984052610
|title=Report: Trump gives Iran Tuesday deadline for deal, threatens 'decapitation'|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=4 August 2026}}</ref>

On 5 August, Trump told Iran to open the Hormuz or be "hit very hard".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.thedailystar.net/news/world/usa/news/trump-warns-iran-open-hormuz-or-get-hit-very-hard-4240546
|title=Trump warns Iran to open Hormuz or get 'hit very hard'|agency=[[Agence France Presse]]|website=[[The Daily Star (Bangladesh)|The Daily Star]]|date=5 August 2026}}</ref>

