=== Iranian losses ===
{{See also|Separatism in Iran|Air campaign in Iranian Kurdistan}}

The US and Israel killed many Iranian commanders and leaders on the war's first day by causing Iran to believe that strikes were not imminent. Thus, groups of senior Iranian officials continued gathering in person. These gatherings were targeted in initial strikes. One part of the deception was information about a US F-22 deployment leaked to hide that preparations were more advanced at other bases.<ref name="Estrin-2026">{{Cite news |last=Estrin |first=Daniel |date=11 March 2026 |title=Old-School Tricks and AI Tech Are Weapons in the Iran War |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/03/10/nx-s1-5741726/israel-iran-war-cyber-ai |access-date=13 April 2026 |work=[[NPR]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Avraham-2026">{{Cite web |last1=Avraham |first1=Yaron |last2=Davori |first2=Nir |last3=Segal |first3=Amit |date=28 February 2026 |script-title=he:30 בכירים איראנים הותקפו בחצי דקה, חלקם הותקפו במקום המסתור |title=30 Bekirim Iranim Hutakfu Bechtzi Dka, Halkam Hutakfu Bemekum Hamistor |trans-title=30 Iranian senior officials attacked in half a minute, after Israeli deception: New details from the opening strike |url=https://www.mako.co.il/news-military/2026_q1/Article-df96fd26975ac91026.htm |access-date=1 March 2026 |website=N12 |language=he}}</ref> Calls between Trump and Netanyahu before the war were not publicised to diminish the possibility of an Iranian first strike.<ref name="Avraham-2026" />

[[IDF Spokesperson's Unit|IDF spokesperson]] Brigadier General [[Effie Defrin]] stated that months of joint US and Israeli "strategic and operational deception" of satellite imagery led up to the war. This encompassed planes and other facilities. The night of the initial strike he and [[Chief of the General Staff (Israel)|IDF Chief of Staff]] Lieutenant General [[Eyal Zamir]] took their official cars home from [[HaKirya|IDF Headquarters]].<ref name="Estrin-2026" /> They came back without them so that satellite imagery would show that their base did not appear full nor warplanes appear armed and ready.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Eichner |first=Itamar |date=28 February 2026 |title=How Israel Pulled off a Second Surprise Against Iran |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/rko5i2ef11l |access-date=9 April 2026 |work=[[Ynet]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Levin |first=Hani |date=28 February 2026 |title=כך הורדמה טהרן: מבצע ההטעיה המתוחכם שסלל את הדרך לתקיפה - בחדרי חרדים |trans-title=This is how Tehran was lulled to sleep: the sophisticated deception operation that paved the way for the attack. |url=https://www.bhol.co.il/news/1720329 |access-date=12 April 2026 |website=Bhol |language=he |trans-quote=The deception operation revealed: What secret moves caused Iranian intelligence to look away at the crucial moment, and how did Israeli-American cooperation create a false image of routine at IDF Headquarters? New details about the sophisticated deception that lulled Tehran to sleep}}</ref> Three separate gatherings of Iranian officials were hit within half a minute of each other in the opening strike.<ref name="Avraham-2026" /> War sources revealed that the American-Israeli strikes targeted IRGC bases, border guard posts, and other security facilities to attempt to allow for potential ground incursions from both [[Iranian–Kurdish conflict|Kurdish separatists to the northwest]] and [[Insurgency in Sistan and Balochistan|Baloch separatists to the southeast]]. There were no reports of cross-border operations from either of the ethnic militant groups, although Iran had engaged in attacks against both of them, reportedly killing both Kurdish and Baloch fighters originating from outside Iran.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Davison|first1=John|last2=McNeill|first2=Ryan|date=8 April 2026|title=Trump's mixed messages and Iran's bombs kept the Kurds out of the war|work=Reuters|url=https://www.reuters.com/investigations/trumps-mixed-messages-irans-bombs-kept-kurds-out-war-2026-04-08/|access-date=1 August 2026}}</ref><ref name="alhurra">{{cite web|last=Hussein|first=Dalshad|date=31 March 2026|title=Baluchistan, A Corridor Under Fire|work=Alhurra|url=https://alhurra.com/en/17443|access-date=1 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Chakraborty|first=Debdutta|date=23 April 2026|title=Iran hits terror group Jaish al-Adl along Pakistan border as Islamabad aims to revive West Asia peace talks|work=ThePrint|url=https://theprint.in/world/iran-hits-terror-group-jaish-al-adl-along-pakistan-border-as-islamabad-aims-to-revive-west-asia-peace-talks/2911951/|access-date=1 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=2 July 2026|title=Revolutionary Guards report deadly clash with Kurdish militants in northwest Iran|work=The Arab Weekly|url=https://thearabweekly.com/revolutionary-guards-report-deadly-clash-kurdish-militants-northwest-iran|access-date=1 August 2026}}</ref>

==== Assassination of Ali Khamenei ====
{{Main|Assassination of Ali Khamenei}}

[[File:Ali Khamenei 2026.02.12 (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|Khamenei on 12 February 2026, 16 days before his assassination]]

On 28 February 2026, [[Ali Khamenei]], the [[supreme leader of Iran]], [[Assassination of Ali Khamenei|was assassinated]] in an Israeli air attack.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/03/04/israel-blue-sparrow-missiles-that-killed-khamenei|title=Israel's jet-launched ballistic missile that took Khamenei by surprise|last=Mendelson|first=Allegra|date=4 March 2026|work=The Telegraph|access-date=18 July 2026}}</ref><ref name="Avraham-2026" /> On 1 March, Iranian state media announced Khamenei's death.<ref>{{cite press release |url=https://farsi.khamenei.ir/news-content?id=62772 |script-title=fa:اطلاعیه شهادت حضرت آیت‌الله العظمی سیدعلی حسینی خامنه‌ای رهبر انقلاب اسلامی |title= |trans-title=Announcement of the martyrdom of His Highness Grand Ayatollah Seyyed Ali Hosseini Khamenei, Leader of the Islamic Revolution |language=fa |work=[[Supreme National Security Council]] |via=KHAMENEI.ir |date=1 March 2026 |access-date=1 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260301023337/https://farsi.khamenei.ir/news-content?id=62772 |archive-date=1 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The IRGC-controlled [[Fars News Agency]] announced that Khamenei's daughter, son-in-law, grandchild, and daughter-in-law [[Zahra Haddad-Adel]] had also been killed.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Habibiazad |first=Ghoncheh |date=1 March 2026 |title=Khamenei's Daughter and Grandchild Killed in Attacks, State Media Says |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn5ge95q6y7t?app-referrer=deep-link&post=asset%3Ae4590a21-5229-434d-be0f-4698491513f8#post |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Khamenei's Relatives Killed in the Attacks Too |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn5ge95q6y7t?app-referrer=deep-link&post=asset%3A6e5ae80b-16ca-45fe-afde-a5e0e3fe5890#post |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Magdy |first=Sam |date=1 March 2026 |title=Khamenei Family Members Killed in Attacks, Fars News Agency Reports |url=https://apnews.com/live/live-updates-israel-iran-february-28-2026#0000019c-a724-d479-ad9e-f76cb5b90000 |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref> The Iranian government declared 40 days of mourning.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=1 March 2026 |title=Iran's Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei Is Dead, State Media Says |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn5ge95q6y7t?post=asset%3Add3db3f8-29d3-4420-a511-9b544b2ea1b0#post |access-date=1 March 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref>

