In Iraq, two members of the Iran-backed [[Popular Mobilization Forces]] (PMF) were killed and three injured in a US-Israeli attack on 28 February.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |title=Two Killed in Israeli Strike on PMF Base in Iraq |url=https://shafaq.com/en/Security/Two-killed-eight-injured-in-Israeli-strike-on-PMF-base-in-Iraq |date=28 February 2026 |access-date=28 February 2026 |website=Shafaq News |language=en}}</ref> A later report estimated three dead.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/02/28/world/iran-strikes-trump/2f9b79e6-a28e-5d7b-b67c-5b95621d953b |first=Erika |last=Solomon |work=[[The New York Times]] |title=U.S. Attacks Iran as Trump Calls for Overthrow of Government |date=28 February 2026}}</ref> On 1 and 2 March, the United States and Israel conducted several attacks on Iranian-backed Iraqi militias to degrade their military capabilities.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Sleiman |first=Nadia |date=3 March 2026 |title=Iran Update Evening Special Report, March 2, 2026 |url=https://understandingwar.org/research/middle-east/iran-update-evening-special-report-march-2-2026/ |access-date=4 March 2026 |website=[[Institute for the Study of War]] |language=en-US}}</ref> 20 former PMF members were killed, and 32 others wounded in the joint US-Saudi Arabia 28 July strike.<ref>.{{#invoke:cite|news|title = US-Saudi strikes in Iraq kill 20 – former paramilitaries|url = https://globalnation.inquirer.net/332974/us-saudi-strikes-in-iraq-kill-20-former-paramilitaries|archive-url = https://ghostarchive.org/archive/YJF6p|archive-date = 29 July 2026|url-status = live|work = Inquirer.net|location = Baghdad|date = 29 July 2026|access-date = 29 July 2026}}</ref>

