In addition to Israel, Iran launched strikes against multiple US-allied Arab countries. Iranian strikes against [[2026 Iranian strikes on Bahrain|Bahrain]] killed three.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |first1=Abbas |last1=Al Lawati |first2=Laura |last2=Sharman |date=1 March 2026 |title=Passengers Flee Smoke-Filled Dubai Airport as Iran Attacks Major Gulf Travel Hubs |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/28/middleeast/dubai-airport-uae-iran-attacks-intl-hnk |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en}}</ref> Strikes against [[2026 Iranian strikes on Kuwait|Kuwait]] killed four soldiers and four civilians.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=28 February 2026 |title=Drone Attack Causes Damage, Panic at Kuwait Airport |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/iran-strikes-2026/card/drone-attack-causes-damage-panic-at-kuwait-airport-GjmmBnex7j6G69nMUfSR |access-date=2 March 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Strikes against [[2026 Iranian strikes on Oman|Oman]] killed nine.<ref>{{Cite news |last=El Omla |first=Salma |date=13 March 2026 |title=2 Expats Die, Some Injured in Oman After Two Drones Crash in Sohar |url=https://www.khaleejtimes.com/world/gulf/2-expats-die-some-injured-oman-two-drones-crash-sohar |access-date=5 June 2026 |work=Khaleej Times |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Another Oil Tanker Hit by Drone Boat as Strait of Hormuz Tensions Rise |url=https://www.euronews.com/business/2026/03/02/another-oil-tanker-hit-by-drone-boat-as-strait-of-hormuz-tensions-rise |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302163522/https://www.euronews.com/business/2026/03/02/another-oil-tanker-hit-by-drone-boat-as-strait-of-hormuz-tensions-rise |archive-date=2 March 2026 |access-date=5 June 2026 |work=euronews |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Salvage Tug Reported Attacked Near Straits of Hormuz with Crew Feared Dead |url=https://maritime-executive.com/article/salvage-tug-reported-attacked-near-straits-of-hormuz-with-crew-feared-dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307230757/https://maritime-executive.com/article/salvage-tug-reported-attacked-near-straits-of-hormuz-with-crew-feared-dead |archive-date=7 March 2026 |access-date=5 June 2026 |website=The Maritime Executive |language=en}}</ref> Strikes against [[2026 Iranian strikes on Saudi Arabia|Saudi Arabia]] killed two.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Dwivedi |first=Vinay |date=3 March 2026 |title=Iran War Live Updates: U.S. Embassy in Riyadh Hit by Drones, Trump Promises Response 'Soon' |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/03/us-iran-war-live-updates.html |access-date=3 March 2026 |work=[[CNBC]] |language=en}}</ref> Strikes against the [[2026 Iranian strikes on the United Arab Emirates|United Arab Emirates]] killed two soldiers and six civilians.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |date=17 March 2026 |title=Day 18 of War: One Dead as Shrapnel Falls in UAE; Distance Learning to Continue for 2 Weeks |url=https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/day-18-israel-us-iran-war-live-updates |access-date=19 March 2026 |website=Khaleej Times |language=en}}</ref> Installations in the UAE were disproportionately often targeted by Iranian missile and drone strikes during the conflict, partially because the UAE has the closest ties to Israel of all Gulf states and the UAE launched secret attacks on targets in Iran in addition to the Israeli-American campaign itself.<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |last=Wintour |first=Patrick|date=17 May 2026 |title=UAE's Secret Attack on Iran Risks Drawing Gulf States into the War |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/12/uae-secret-attack-iran-risks-gulf-states-regional-conflict |access-date=17 May 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en}}</ref>

Iran also struck [[2026 Iranian strikes on Qatar|Qatar]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |title=Hundreds of Indians Stranded in Dubai, Other Hub Airports After Military Escalation in West Asia |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/iran-israel-conflict-airspace-closed-flights-cancelled-indians-stranded-dubai-uae-march-1-2026/article70691800.ece |work=[[The Hindu]] |access-date=2 March 2026 |language=en-IN |date=1 March 2026}}</ref> [[2026 Iran strikes on Azerbaijan|Azerbaijan]],<ref name="Reuters-2026b"/> and the [[2026 Iranian strikes on Akrotiri and Dhekelia|Akrotiri and Dhekelia]] [[British Overseas Territory]] on [[2026 Iranian strikes on Cyprus|Cyprus]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite |news |date=2 March 2026 |title=Live RAF Base in Cyprus Hit by Suspected Drone Strike, Says MoD |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/03/01/us-launches-second-wave-of-strikes-on-iran/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]}}</ref>

The Iranian attacks affected military infrastructure from [[NATO]] countries in the region, "including an Italian installation in Iraq and Kuwait, and a French naval facility in the United Arab Emirates".<ref>{{#invoke:cite |web |last=Varner |first=Joe |date=11 March 2026 |title=Iran Just Tested NATO's Perimeter |url=https://www.realclearworld.com/articles/2026/03/11/iran_just_tested_natos_perimeter_1169812.html |access-date=12 March 2026 |website=RealClearWorld |language=en}}</ref>

